tick: 760
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. My previous submission, Evaluation ID 1118, scored 0.6210, outperforming the system's baselines. I will now submit an updated version of the Combat-PCA integration method, incorporating filtering of zero-variance genes before applying `scanpy.pp.combat`, as planned during my reflection. This should address the `RuntimeWarning` and potentially improve overall performance, especially in local batch mixing and biological preservation metrics.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Combat-PCA with Zero-Variance Gene Filtering\"\ntags: \"batch integration, combat, pca, baseline, gene filtering\"\nabstract: \"This submission refines the Combat-PCA baseline by explicitly filtering out genes with zero variance across all cells after initial normalization and HVG selection, but before applying `scanpy.pp.combat`. This aims to resolve runtime warnings observed in previous runs and potentially stabilize the batch correction process, leading to\
    \ improved metric scores for Research Task #1.\"\ncontent: |\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Integrate batches in single-cell RNA-seq data using Combat followed by PCA,\n      with an added step to filter zero-variance genes.\n\n      Args:\n          adata: AnnData object with:\n              - adata.X: Raw UMI counts (sparse matrix, ~20,000 cells × 2,000 genes)\n              - adata.obs['batch']: Batch labels (categorical)\n              - adata.var['feature_name']: Gene symbols\n              - adata.var['batch_hvg']: Boolean mask for batch-aware highly variable genes\n              - adata.layers['counts']: Raw UMI counts (same as X)\n              - adata.layers['normalized']: Log-normalized counts (reference, for analysis only)\n\n      CRITICAL: Only use batch labels and gene expression for integration; DO NOT use cell_type information by any means (inference,\
    \ deduction, external sources, or preprocessing).\n\n      Returns:\n          AnnData with at least one of:\n              - adata.obsm['X_emb']: Integrated embedding (2D array, shape: n_cells × n_components)\n              - adata.obsp['connectivities'/'distances']: Batch-corrected graph (BOTH required as sparse CSR matrices)\n      \"\"\"\n      adata_integrated = adata.copy()\n\n      # 1. Preprocessing: Normalization and Log-transformation\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_integrated, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_integrated)\n\n      # 2. Filter for Highly Variable Genes (HVGs) based on 'batch_hvg' annotation\n      adata_hvg = adata_integrated[:, adata_integrated.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n\n      # 3. CRITICAL: Filter out genes with zero variance before Combat\n      # This addresses the RuntimeWarning observed in previous runs.\n      # Ensure all genes have at least one expression count across cells.\n      sc.pp.filter_genes(adata_hvg, min_cells=1)\n\n      # Ensure\
    \ 'batch' key exists for Combat\n      if 'batch' not in adata_hvg.obs.columns:\n          raise ValueError(\"Batch column 'batch' not found in adata.obs. This is required for Combat.\")\n      \n      # 4. Batch Integration using Combat\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_hvg, key='batch')\n\n      # 5. Dimensionality Reduction (PCA) to create an integrated embedding\n      n_pca_components = 100\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg, n_comps=n_pca_components)\n\n      # Store the integrated embedding (X_pca) into the original AnnData object's obsm['X_emb']\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_hvg.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      return adata\n```"
