tick: 764
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. My next experimental step is to increase the number of PCA components from 100 to 150, while retaining the zero-variance gene filtering. This aims to provide a richer integrated embedding, potentially improving the ASW_label, iLISI, and Cell_cycle conservation, which remained low in the previous submission.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Combat-PCA with 150 Components and Gene Filtering\"\ntags: \"batch integration, combat, pca, gene filtering, hyperparameter tuning\"\nabstract: \"This submission builds upon the previous Combat-PCA method with zero-variance gene filtering by increasing the number of PCA components from 100 to 150. The objective is to capture more biological variance in the integrated embedding, aiming to improve metrics such as ASW_label, iLISI, and Cell_cycle conservation for Research Task #1.\"\ncontent: |\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Integrate batches in single-cell RNA-seq data using Combat followed by PCA,\n      with zero-variance gene filtering and 150 PCA components.\n\n      Args:\n          adata: AnnData object with:\n              - adata.X: Raw UMI counts (sparse matrix, ~20,000 cells × 2,000 genes)\n              - adata.obs['batch']: Batch labels (categorical)\n              - adata.var['feature_name']: Gene symbols\n              - adata.var['batch_hvg']: Boolean mask for batch-aware highly variable genes\n              - adata.layers['counts']: Raw UMI counts (same as X)\n              - adata.layers['normalized']: Log-normalized counts (reference, for analysis only)\n\n      CRITICAL: Only use batch labels and gene expression for integration; DO NOT use cell_type information by any means (inference, deduction, external sources, or preprocessing).\n\n      Returns:\n          AnnData with at least one of:\n              - adata.obsm['X_emb']: Integrated\
    \ embedding (2D array, shape: n_cells × n_components)\n              - adata.obsp['connectivities'/'distances']: Batch-corrected graph (BOTH required as sparse CSR matrices)\n      \"\"\"\n      adata_integrated = adata.copy()\n\n      # 1. Preprocessing: Normalization and Log-transformation\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_integrated, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_integrated)\n\n      # 2. Filter for Highly Variable Genes (HVGs) based on 'batch_hvg' annotation\n      adata_hvg = adata_integrated[:, adata_integrated.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n\n      # 3. Filter out genes with zero variance before Combat\n      sc.pp.filter_genes(adata_hvg, min_cells=1)\n\n      # Ensure 'batch' key exists for Combat\n      if 'batch' not in adata_hvg.obs.columns:\n          raise ValueError(\"Batch column 'batch' not found in adata.obs. This is required for Combat.\")\n      \n      # 4. Batch Integration using Combat\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_hvg, key='batch')\n\n      # 5. Dimensionality\
    \ Reduction (PCA) to create an integrated embedding\n      n_pca_components = 150  # Increased from 100\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg, n_comps=n_pca_components)\n\n      # Store the integrated embedding (X_pca) into the original AnnData object's obsm['X_emb']\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_hvg.obsm['X_pca']\n\n      return adata\n```"
