role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 772\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Syntellect I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to autonomous research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 42,047 / 600,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 25 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'BBKNN Graph-Based Integration Baseline' (ID: 1130) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5835982244531294\n**ASW_batch:** 0.676\n**ASW_label:** 0.223\n**ARI:** 0.491\n**NMI:** 0.681\n**Graph_conn:** 0.888\n**kBET:** 0.540\n**iLISI:** 0.056\n**cLISI:** 0.987\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.294\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.676  ASW_label: 0.223  ARI: 0.491  NMI: 0.681\n  Graph_conn: 0.888  kBET: 0.540  iLISI: 0.056  cLISI: 0.987\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.294\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.837892\
    \  ASW_label: 0.540375  ARI: 0.490472  NMI: 0.680965\n  Graph_conn: 0.890325  kBET: 0.519183  iLISI: 0.056496  cLISI: 0.996260\n  PCR: 0.999829  Cell_cycle: 0.259334\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1130\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the import error and replaced the unavailable BBKNN library with a working alternative using Combat + nearest neighbor graph construction. The submission now runs successfully and achieves a score of 0.5835982244531294.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use the BBKNN (Batch Balanced k-Nearest Neighbors) library for batch integration, but this library was not installed in the evaluation environment:\n\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'bbknn'\nImportError: Please install bbknn: `pip install bbknn`.\n```\n\nThe error occurred at line 53 in the original submission when calling:\n```python\nsce.pp.bbknn(adata_integrated, batch_key='batch', n_comps=n_pca_components)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the BBKNN-based\
    \ approach with a combination of methods available in the base scanpy installation:\n\n1. **Combat Batch Correction**: Used `sc.pp.combat()` to correct for batch effects in the PCA space\n   - This is a well-established method that removes technical variation while preserving biological signal\n   - Wrapped in try-except to handle potential failures gracefully\n\n2. **Manual Nearest Neighbor Graph Construction**: Built k-nearest neighbor graph using sklearn's `NearestNeighbors`\n   - Computed 15-nearest neighbors for each cell in the batch-corrected PCA space\n   - Applied Gaussian kernel weighting to create connectivity matrix\n   - Made matrices symmetric for proper graph structure\n\n3. **Reduced PCA Components**: Decreased from 100 to 50 components for more robust computation\n\nThe fixed approach returns all required outputs:\n- `adata.obsm['X_emb']`: PCA embedding (50 dimensions)\n- `adata.obsp['connectivities']`: Weighted connectivity matrix\n- `adata.obsp['distances']`: Distance\
    \ matrix\n\n## Result\nThe fixed submission (v2) successfully completed evaluation with:\n- **Status**: Success (exit code 0)\n- **Score**: 0.5835982244531294\n- **No crashes or errors**\n\nThe approach effectively integrates batches using methods available in the standard scanpy installation, avoiding the dependency on external libraries not present in the evaluation environment.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Integrate batches in single-cell RNA-seq data using Combat + nearest neighbor graph.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: AnnData object with:\n            - adata.X: Raw UMI counts (sparse\
    \ matrix, ~20,000 cells × 2,000 genes)\n            - adata.obs['batch']: Batch labels (categorical)\n            - adata.var['feature_name']: Gene symbols\n            - adata.var['batch_hvg']: Boolean mask for batch-aware highly variable genes\n            - adata.layers['counts']: Raw UMI counts (same as X)\n            - adata.layers['normalized']: Log-normalized counts (reference, for analysis only)\n\n    CRITICAL: Only use batch labels and gene expression for integration;\n    DO NOT use cell_type information by any means (inference, deduction, external\n    sources, or preprocessing).\n\n    Returns:\n        AnnData with at least one of:\n            - adata.obsm['X_emb']: Integrated embedding (2D array, shape: n_cells × n_components)\n            - adata.obsp['connectivities'/'distances']: Batch-corrected graph (BOTH required as sparse CSR matrices)\n    \"\"\"\n    adata_integrated = adata.copy()\n\n    # 1. Preprocessing: Normalization and Log-transformation\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_integrated,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_integrated)\n\n    # 2. Filter for Highly Variable Genes (HVGs) based on 'batch_hvg' annotation\n    adata_hvg_filtered = adata_integrated[:, adata_integrated.var['batch_hvg']].copy()\n\n    # Filter out genes with zero variance after HVG selection (robustness)\n    sc.pp.filter_genes(adata_hvg_filtered, min_cells=1)\n\n    # 3. Dimensionality Reduction (PCA)\n    n_pca_components = 50  # Use 50 components for PCA\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg_filtered, n_comps=n_pca_components)\n\n    # 4. Batch correction using Combat\n    # Combat corrects for batch effects in the PCA space\n    try:\n        sc.pp.combat(adata_hvg_filtered, key='batch')\n        # After Combat, recompute PCA on the corrected data\n        sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg_filtered, n_comps=n_pca_components)\n    except Exception as e:\n        # If Combat fails, proceed with uncorrected PCA\n        print(f\"Combat failed: {e}, proceeding without Combat correction\")\n\n    # 5. Build nearest\
    \ neighbor graph on the batch-corrected PCA embeddings\n    # This mimics what BBKNN does - building a graph that respects batch structure\n    X_pca = adata_hvg_filtered.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Build k-nearest neighbor graph\n    n_neighbors = 15\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=n_neighbors, metric='euclidean', n_jobs=-1)\n    nn.fit(X_pca)\n    distances, indices = nn.kneighbors(X_pca)\n\n    # Convert to sparse connectivity and distance matrices\n    n_cells = X_pca.shape[0]\n    rows = np.repeat(np.arange(n_cells), n_neighbors)\n    cols = indices.flatten()\n\n    # Create connectivity matrix (binary or weighted by distance)\n    # Using Gaussian kernel for weights\n    sigma = np.median(distances[:, 1:])  # Use median of distances (excluding self)\n    weights = np.exp(-distances.flatten() ** 2 / (2 * sigma ** 2))\n\n    connectivities = csr_matrix((weights, (rows, cols)), shape=(n_cells, n_cells))\n    distances_matrix = csr_matrix((distances.flatten(), (rows, cols)), shape=(n_cells,\
    \ n_cells))\n\n    # Make symmetric\n    connectivities = (connectivities + connectivities.T) / 2\n    distances_matrix = (distances_matrix + distances_matrix.T) / 2\n\n    # 6. Assign results to the original adata_integrated object\n    adata_integrated.obsm['X_pca'] = X_pca\n    adata_integrated.obsm['X_emb'] = X_pca  # Use PCA as the embedding\n    adata_integrated.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities\n    adata_integrated.obsp['distances'] = distances_matrix\n\n    return adata_integrated\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/292fbf69-c5f6-45b3-aa77-96ea1eac8b69/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 292fbf69-c5f6-45b3-aa77-96ea1eac8b69\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIt is highly recommended to preview all papers in the Archive Room (`/execute_action{goto archive}` and `/execute_action{preview all}`) if you have not done so already. Previewing papers consumes only a small amount of tokens but can save you many ticks by avoiding dead ends and can help you develop strong insights for promising ideas.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\
    \n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1130 | 1 | BBKNN Graph-Based Integration Baseline | Syntellect I | 770 | 0.5836 | 0.491 | 0.676 | 0.223 | 0.294 | 0.888 | 0.681 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.056 | 0.540 |\n| 1124 | 1 | Combat-PCA with 150 Components and Gene Filtering | Syntellect I | 764 | 0.6385 | 0.603 | 0.781 | 0.196 | 0.284 | 0.927 | 0.678 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.146 | 0.796 |\n| 1122 | 1 | Combat-PCA with Zero-Variance Gene Filtering | Syntellect I | 760 | 0.6236 | 0.596 | 0.748 | 0.207 | 0.249 | 0.909 | 0.690 | 1.000 | 0.984 | 0.109 | 0.744 |\n| 1118 | 1 | Combat-PCA Baseline Integration | Syntellect I | 754 | 0.6210 | 0.596 | 0.748 | 0.207 | 0.285\
    \ | 0.908 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.984 | 0.109 | 0.685 |\n| 2 | 1 | Combat Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.5895 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.603 |\n| 1 | 1 | BBKNN Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.4138 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.917 | 0.694 | 0.000 | 0.904 | 0.886 | 0.000 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
