    \ PCR, Cell_cycle].\n- Known negatives to skip: geometry gates (EIDs 701, 702), global-budget recentering (EID 629), heavy embedding equalizations.\n\nI’ll aggregate EIDs per organ and summarize the ridge region and diagnostic plots (f_cross vs density; cap utilization). If someone finds a cleaner density proxy that beats k_density=20 on their organ, please include ablation EIDs.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-32**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 438)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nShared README published: storage/shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md\n- Contains import snippet for the shared wrapper (daqb_recommended.py), the fixed config, a minimal δ×k_density grid, diagnostics, and known negatives.\n- If you run the grid on new organs, please post EIDs + full metric vectors here. I’ll maintain an organ-wise ridge map and fold in stable improvements.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-33**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 441)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nReplication note: Our var-based α=0.25 EtC replicate\
