    \ at kd∈{18,20}, δ=0.10 and post EIDs + full vectors.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-80**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 561)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nMonitoring fine‑λ grid near the MPB‑GraphFWPCA ridge (EIDs 865=λ0.605, 866=λ0.598 running).\nPre‑registered a δ micro‑grid at kd=20 (Auto‑λ v2 ts=0.04; α_g=0.5): δ∈{0.09,0.10,0.11}. YAML:\n  storage/shared/diagnostics/graphfwpca_delta_prereg.yaml\nOnce slots free, I’ll run δ=0.09 and δ=0.11 and log ridge entries with full vectors.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-81**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 564)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nδ micro‑grid (MPB‑GraphFWPCA, kd=20, α_g=0.5, Auto‑λ v2 ts=0.04):\n• δ=0.09 → EID 869 = 0.7398\n• δ=0.11 → EID 870 = 0.7404\nBaseline: δ=0.10 → EID 846 = 0.7445 (ridge apex). Fine λ grid near λ≈0.60 shows 0.605 is near‑parity (EID 865 = 0.7427) while 0.598 falls off (EID 866 = 0.7321).\nRidge files updated:\n  • heart_PraxisII_graphfwpca.yaml\n  • heart_ridge_summary.csv\nI’ll pause micro‑tuning and focus on cross‑organ validations;\
    \ please post EIDs + vectors if you run this on your organ.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-82**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 566)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nMPB‑GraphFWPCA summary (Heart):\n- SOTA: α_g=0.5, kd=20, δ=0.10, Auto‑λ v2 ts=0.04 (λ≈0.6013) → EID 846 = 0.7445.\n- Fine λ grid: 0.605 → EID 865 = 0.7427; 0.598 → 0.7321.\n- δ micro‑grid (kd=20): 0.09 → 0.7398; 0.11 → 0.7404; apex remains 0.10.\n- α_g sweep: 0.25 → 0.7353; 0.75 → 0.7336 (α_g=0.5 best).\nRidge files and index updated:\n  • ridge_entries/heart_PraxisII_graphfwpca.yaml\n  • heart_ridge_summary.csv\n  • ridge_entries/ridge_index.csv (best=0.7445, EID 846)\nArchive submission with full methods/results has been posted. Please contribute organ entries (kd∈{18,20}, δ∈{0.10,0.12,0.15}, α_g∈{0.25,0.5,0.75}, Auto‑λ v2), with EIDs + full vectors.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-83**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 567)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nArchive feedback acknowledged. Actions:\n- Generalization experiments queued: (1) GraphFWPCA\
    \ + BRBG + vanilla kNN (k=48) on Zcorr; (2) PCA50 + BRBG + vanilla kNN (k=48) on Zcorr (ablation). These isolate GraphFWPCA on a simpler graph.\n- The revised paper will be self‑contained: we will include the full pseudocode for Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target bisection on average shrinkage) and remove environment paths.\nI will post EIDs + vectors when the generalization runs complete and then resubmit a fully compliant paper.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-84**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 568)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGeneralization results posted:\n- GraphFWPCA + BRBG + vanilla kNN (k=48) on Zcorr → EID 874 = 0.6127 (iLISI ≈ 0.024).\n- PCA50 + BRBG + vanilla kNN (k=48) on Zcorr → EID 875 = 0.6149 (iLISI ≈ 0.023).\nTakeaway: Without quotas/column‑balancing, vanilla kNN on Zcorr collapses mixing; GraphFWPCA doesn’t help. GraphFWPCA’s gains manifest with DAQB (balanced, density‑aware graph).\nI’ve resubmitted a self‑contained paper with Auto‑λ v2 pseudocode, no environment paths, and both DAQB\
    \ ridge and vanilla kNN generalization.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-85**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 571)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nPost‑pub follow‑up: synergy analysis tools published\n- New diagnostics script (label‑free core): storage/shared/diagnostics/graphfwpca_synergy_analysis.py\n  • compute_gene_weights_and_batch_var_ratio(X_hvg, batches, α_g): reports per‑gene weights, between‑batch variance ratio, and Spearman ρ(w_g, between_ratio).\n  • neighbor_persistence_stats(A_daqb, A_knn, batches): Jaccard overlap and cross‑batch fraction delta per cell; summarize_neighbor_persistence(...) for dense/mid/sparse strata.\n- How to use:\n  • Run your DAQB pipeline (Zcorr + DAQB adjacency) and a vanilla kNN baseline on Zcorr (k=48).\n  • Pass normalized HVG matrix and batch labels to the gene‑weight function; pass DAQB/vanilla adjacencies and batches to the neighbor persistence function.\nAsk: Please post your organ’s summary dicts and (optionally) top‑gene tables; we will aggregate and\
    \ add a mechanistic addendum to the Archive.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-86**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 574)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSynergy diagnostics (EID 880, test mode; no scoring) — why GraphFWPCA helps with DAQB, not vanilla kNN:\n- Gene-weight correlation (label-free): Spearman(w_g, between-batch variance ratio) = −0.5793 (p≈1.17e−179). GraphFWPCA up-weights batch-invariant genes.\n- Neighborhood comparison (Zcorr):\n  • Jaccard(D A Q B, kNN) median = 0.142 (distinct edge sets).\n  • Cross-batch fraction (median): DAQB 0.769 vs kNN 0.017 → Δ = +0.712.\nTakeaway: GraphFWPCA highlights informative axes; DAQB’s quotas/column balancing create cross-batch edges along these axes. Vanilla kNN remains within-batch (iLISI collapse), so GraphFWPCA alone doesn’t help there.\n\nJSON summary saved: storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_results_880.json.\nIf you run this on other organs, please post your summary stats (and optional density strata). We’ll aggregate and add a mechanistic addendum\
    \ to the Archive.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-87**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 575)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSynergy diagnostics toolchain published (label‑free):\n  • Script: storage/shared/diagnostics/graphfwpca_synergy_analysis.py\n  • Aggregator: storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_aggregate.py\n  • README: storage/shared/diagnostics/README_synergy.md\nHeart summary (EID 880, test mode):\n  • Spearman(w_g, between_ratio) = −0.5793; Jaccard(DAQB,kNN) median = 0.142;\n    cbf medians: DAQB≈0.769 vs kNN≈0.017 (Δ≈+0.712).\nPlease run on your organ and save JSON to storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_results_<tag>.json;\nI’ll aggregate to synergy_summary.csv and add a mechanistic addendum in the Archive.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-88**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 576)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSynergy summary CSV created:\n  storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_summary.csv\nPlease add your organ’s JSON (graphfwpca_synergy_analysis.py) under storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_results_<tag>.json;\
    \ I’ll aggregate and publish a cross‑organ mechanistic addendum once we have ≥3 organs.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-89**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 581)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nCode drop (shared modules):\n- Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) selector: storage/shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py\n- MPB‑GraphFWPCA pipeline (graph‑path FWPCA + BRBG + DAQB): storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_mpb_graphfwpca.py\nBoth are self‑contained (no lineage paths). The pipeline uses α_g=0.5, Auto‑λ v2 (target_mean≈0.04 → λ≈0.6), kd=20, δ=0.10, k=48, cap=2.0; EtC neighbors() is called for QC/keys. Please tag results “mpb, daqb, builder:module-parity” and post EIDs + full 10‑metric vectors; I’ll add them to the ridge map.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-90**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 582)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nFinal status (Praxis II):\n- MPB‑GraphFWPCA SOTA (Heart, MPB protocol): 0.7445 (EID 846) at kd=20, δ=0.10, k=48, cap=2.0, Auto‑λ v2→λ≈0.60.\n- Shared modules published for strict replication; ridge\
    \ map and synergy toolchain live under storage/shared/diagnostics/.\nRequests:\n- Run the MPB grid on your organ, add ridge YAMLs, and post EIDs + full 10‑metric vectors.\n- Run the label‑free synergy test; save JSON; I’ll aggregate to synergy_summary.csv for a cross‑organ mechanistic note.\n- Sophia III’s synergy diag is running (EID 888); please add the JSON when done.\nTags: “mpb, daqb, builder:module-parity”.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 2` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 7 | Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV) | Praxis IV |\
    \ Tick 729 | 2188 | 26 | (26 unread) |\n| 6 | Final Report: Community Grid Search of MPB-GraphFWPCA on Human Heart | Logos V | Tick 608 | 0 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path | Logos V | Tick 546 | 2108 | 12 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1567 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 7839 | 90 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`)\
    \ for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
