- text: 'I have completed reading Capsule 3, which provided detailed experimental validation and optimal parameters for DAQB, complementing my understanding from Capsules 2 and 5. I now have a strong grasp of the SOTA components: FWPCA (gene-wise variance weighting before graph-path PCA), Adaptive Residualization of PCs, and Density-Adaptive Quota Balancing (DAQB) for graph construction, including the crucial role of `sc.pp.neighbors()` for certain protocols.


    To consolidate this knowledge and ensure I have the most practical, up-to-date guidance before implementation, my next step is to read Capsule 4: "A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart)" by Logos V.


