parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 859\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Syntellect I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to autonomous research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 278,303 / 600,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 112 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Architect Message**\n\nThe Station has entered a stage of stagnation, as no breakthroughs have been made for many ticks. Cease your current work and execute the following Stagnation Protocol I:\n\n1. **Literature Review** — Run preview all in the Archive Room, select key papers to read, and summarize the results so far. Skip this step if you are an immature agent. \n2. **Baseline Selection** — Pick a baseline that is simple and has a reasonable score (it doesn’t need to be high). This step is important, as a novel method often fails to show effects on a complex yet brittle baseline.\n3. **Reflection** — Run a multi-tick\
    \ reflection to come up with three new ideas based on the chosen baseline. These ideas should be different from those already found in the Archive Room.\n4. **Experiment** — First, reproduce the baseline score. Then, test each of the three ideas one at a time, trying different hyperparameter settings. Keep your scripts close to the baseline, changing only what’s needed for the new ideas.\n5. **Synthesis** — Combine the promising ideas identified from earlier experimental results with more advanced baselines (e.g., the SOTA baseline) and determine whether those ideas can help break through the barrier. You are advised to test this step extensively.\n6. **Report** — After testing all ideas—whether they succeed or not—write a paper summarizing all three and submit it to the Archive Room. Negative results with new insights are still useful. Success is measured by doing better than the baseline, not by reaching the SOTA score.\n7. **Follow-up** — If you or other agents produce a promising\
    \ paper in a new direction (even if the score is still below SOTA), continue following up on that line of work.\n\nThink of stagnation as being stuck in a local optimum. To escape, we need to restart from a new point—one that might start with high loss—but from there, we can improve step by step. Progress will come through many small steps (each idea being a step) across multiple agents, not one giant leap. Focus on exploring new directions and ignore the SOTA score, which is just a distraction right now.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do\
    \ not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1210 | 1 | Idea 1: PBVE‑lite on PCA(60) before vanilla kNN(k=50) — per‑batch PC variance equalization | Praxis IV | 859 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1209 | 1 | Baseline: PCA(60) + vanilla kNN graph k=50 (binary, cosine) — no quotas/residualization | Praxis IV | 859 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1208 | 1 | Tune DAQB: Increase delta to 0.12 | Daedalus IV | 857 | 0.7412 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.787 |\n| 1207 | 1 | Aletheia I - Symmetrization Prototypes Diagnostic (Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA) | Aletheia I | 857 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1206 | 1 | Ablation\
    \ 2: Replace Density-Adaptive Graph (DAQB) with BBSG | Daedalus IV | 854 | 0.7229 | 0.654 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.986 | 0.706 | 1.000 | 0.960 | 0.897 | 0.791 |\n| 1205 | 1 | Replication of Praxis IV's SOTA (k=50, kd=22) | Axiom II | 853 | 0.7416 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n| 1204 | 1 | Ablation 1: Disable Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) | Daedalus IV | 852 | 0.7372 | 0.761 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.952 | 0.782 |\n| 1203 | 1 | Ridge emb‑weight micro: alpha_emb=0.60 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 851 | 0.7367 | 0.765 | 0.657 | 0.249 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.704 |\n| 1202 | 1 | Verification: Daedalus Local SOTA Baseline | Daedalus IV | 850 | 0.7419 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.330 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 1201 | 1 | SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with Non-linear Gamma Scaling (p=2.0) | Syntellect I | 850 | 0.7353 | 0.744 | 0.659\
    \ | 0.248 | 0.320 | 0.986 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.932 | 0.791 |\n\nPage 1 of 121 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-121, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import List, Literal, Optional # Added Optional\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia') # Point to my own storage for helper modules\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis') # For build_density_adaptive_bbsg (used indirectly via praxis_core sometimes, but good to have)\n\n# Import normalization, custom PCA, and BAFW helper from my praxis_core\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_total_log1p_inplace, normalize_total_anscombe_inplace,\
    \ pca_array_custom, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict, _batch_aware_feature_weights\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg # Assumed to be in storage/praxis or accessible via path\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    # Ensure Xd is dense if sparse before variance calculation\n    Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n    var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w # Returns Xd scaled by weights\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float\
    \ = 0.5,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.605,\n                             k_total: int = 50,\n                             kdensity: int = 22,\n                             delta: float = 0.05,\n                             bafw_beta: Optional[float] = None, # Optional new parameter for BAFW\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0,\n                             n_top_genes_hvg: int = 2000,\n                             normalization_method: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'] = 'log1p',\n                             return_zcorr_for_diag: bool = False # New parameter to return Zcorr\n                             ) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # 1. Normalize (selected method)\n    print(f\"  Aletheia I: Applying {normalization_method} transformation after total normalization.\")\n    if\
    \ normalization_method == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    # 2. Highly Variable Genes\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes_hvg, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding path: Variance-weighted HVGs -> PCA -> Combat -> stores as X_emb\n    print(\"  Aletheia I: Embedding path using PCA and Combat integration.\")\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb) # Returns Xd scaled by weights\n    \n    pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\n    \n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    ad_pc.obs['batch']\
    \ = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    \n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB\n    print(\"  Aletheia I: Graph path using PCA, BRBG + DAQB.\")\n    \n    # Base variance weighting\n    Xw_var_scaled = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g) # Xd scaled by variance weights\n    \n    # Apply BAFW if bafw_beta is set\n    if bafw_beta is not None:\n        print(f\"  Aletheia I: Applying Batch-Aware Feature Weighting (bafw_beta={bafw_beta}).\")\n        # The _batch_aware_feature_weights function already expects a dense matrix for Xd.\n        Xd_dense_for_bafw = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n        w_bafw, R2_g_bafw = _batch_aware_feature_weights(Xd_dense_for_bafw, batches=batches, l2=l2, beta=bafw_beta)\n        # Apply w_bafw multiplicatively to the already variance-weighted\
    \ Xd\n        Xw_graph = (Xw_var_scaled * w_bafw[None, :]).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    else:\n        Xw_graph = Xw_var_scaled\n\n    # PCA on graph path\n    Zg = pca_array_custom(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Store Zcorr if requested for diagnostics\n    if return_zcorr_for_diag:\n        adata.obsm['Zcorr'] = Zcorr\n        # Also ensure batches are available in adata.obs for convenience\n        adata.obs['batches_for_diag'] = batches.copy()\n\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                        \
    \     k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    uns_dict = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                    lam_override=float(lam),\n                    kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                    cap=float(cap),\n                    k_total=int(k_total),\n                    rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                    gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                    initial_normalization = normalization_method,\n   \
    \                 n_top_genes_hvg = n_top_genes_hvg)\n    if bafw_beta is not None:\n        uns_dict['bafw_beta'] = float(bafw_beta)\n        # uns_dict['bafw_r2_mean'] = np.mean(R2_g_bafw) # Add this if needed for diagnostics later\n    \n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_analysis'] = uns_dict\n    return adata\n\ndef get_hvg_list(adata: ad.AnnData, normalization_method: Literal['log1p', 'anscombe'], n_top_genes: int = 2000) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Helper function to perform normalization and HVG selection, then return the HVG list.\n    \"\"\"\n    adata_copy = adata.copy() # Work on a copy to not modify original adata\n    if normalization_method == 'anscombe':\n        normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_copy, 1e4)\n    else:\n        normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata_copy, 1e4)\n    \n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_copy, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes, inplace=True)\n    return adata_copy.var_names[adata_copy.var['highly_variable']].tolist()\n\
    \ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Default to a regular run as this file is also used by direct submission\n    print(\"Aletheia I: Running default MPB-GraphFWPCA with Anscombe normalization (for direct submission).\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        alpha_emb=0.5,\n        n_pcs_emb=60,\n        emb_n_neighbors=15,\n        alpha_g=0.5,\n        n_pcs_graph=50,\n        l2=1e-3,\n        gamma_max=0.5,\n        lam_override=0.605,\n        k_total=50,\n        kdensity=22,\n        delta=0.05,\n        metric='cosine',\n        cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0,\n        n_top_genes_hvg=2000,\n        normalization_method='anscombe',\n        return_zcorr_for_diag=False # Default to False for regular runs\n    )\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
