- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 860\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Syntellect I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to autonomous research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 284,377 / 600,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 113 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nExplicitly state your identity, current location, and a brief recap of recent events at the beginning of each response. Always include a verbose, general reflection on past events and future plans.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/aletheia/praxis_core.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/aletheia/praxis_core.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq\
    \ Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1210 | 1 | Idea 1: PBVE‑lite on PCA(60) before vanilla kNN(k=50) — per‑batch PC variance equalization | Praxis IV | 859 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1209 | 1 | Baseline: PCA(60) + vanilla kNN graph k=50 (binary, cosine) — no quotas/residualization | Praxis IV | 859 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1208 | 1 | Tune DAQB: Increase delta to 0.12 | Daedalus IV | 857 | 0.7412 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.787 |\n| 1207 | 1 | Aletheia I - Symmetrization Prototypes Diagnostic (Anscombe-MPB-GraphFWPCA) | Aletheia I | 857\
    \ | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1206 | 1 | Ablation 2: Replace Density-Adaptive Graph (DAQB) with BBSG | Daedalus IV | 854 | 0.7229 | 0.654 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.986 | 0.706 | 1.000 | 0.960 | 0.897 | 0.791 |\n| 1205 | 1 | Replication of Praxis IV's SOTA (k=50, kd=22) | Axiom II | 853 | 0.7416 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.791 |\n| 1204 | 1 | Ablation 1: Disable Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) | Daedalus IV | 852 | 0.7372 | 0.761 | 0.681 | 0.218 | 0.352 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.952 | 0.782 |\n| 1203 | 1 | Ridge emb‑weight micro: alpha_emb=0.60 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 851 | 0.7367 | 0.765 | 0.657 | 0.249 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.704 |\n| 1202 | 1 | Verification: Daedalus Local SOTA Baseline | Daedalus IV | 850 | 0.7419 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.330 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 1201 | 1 | SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with Non-linear Gamma\
    \ Scaling (p=2.0) | Syntellect I | 850 | 0.7353 | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.320 | 0.986 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.932 | 0.791 |\n\nPage 1 of 121 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-121, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/aletheia/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_total_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X.data = np.sqrt(adata.X.data + 3/8).astype(np.float32)\n    else:\n        adata.X = np.sqrt(adata.X + 3/8).astype(np.float32)\n\ndef pca_array_custom(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    pca = PCA(n_components=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    pca.fit(Xd)\n    return pca.transform(Xd).astype(np.float32)\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n\
    \    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n    p_exp: float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array_custom(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n   \
    \ else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap: float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\ndef _batch_aware_feature_weights(Xd: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3, beta: float = 0.50):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute batch-aware per-gene weights from ridge regression of gene expression on batch one-hots.\n    w_bafw_g = (1 - R2_g)^beta, where R2_g uses variance explained by batch prediction.\n    \"\"\"\n    # One-hot batches\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B = np.zeros((Xd.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(np.float32)\n\n    # Solve ridge for all genes at once: W (nb x genes)\n    # Handle sparse Xd correctly for @ operator\n    if sp.issparse(Xd):\n        Xd_dense = Xd.toarray() # Convert to dense for @ if sparse\n    else:\n        Xd_dense = Xd\n\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Xd_dense)  # (nb x genes)\n    Zhat = B @ W  # (n x genes) predictions\n\n    var_total = Xd_dense.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    # prediction variance (non-negative)\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    w_bafw = np.power(1.0 - R2 + 1e-8, beta).astype(np.float32)\n    return w_bafw, R2\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 860
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. I have successfully read `storage/aletheia/praxis_core.py`, which defines the `_batch_aware_feature_weights` function.\n\n**Understanding BAFW (`_batch_aware_feature_weights`):**\n*   It computes `R2_g` for each gene, representing the variance explained by batch identity.\n*   The weight `w_bafw = (1.0 - R2_g)**beta`.\n*   **Interpretation:** Genes whose expression is *less explained by batch* (low `R2_g`) will have higher weights, as `1-R2_g` will be closer to 1. Conversely, genes strongly explained by batch (high `R2_g`) will have lower weights. The `beta` parameter controls the steepness of this weighting.\n*   This is conceptually sound for preserving biological signal: up-weighting genes that are robust to batch effects.\n\n**Revisiting Stagnation Protocol I:**\nI have completed Steps 1 (Literature Review) and 2 (Baseline Selection). I previously outlined three new ideas in my reflection (Tick 858). I am now ready to proceed with **Step 4: Experiment**.\n\
    \n**Implementing Idea 1: Integration of BAFW into `log1p`-based SOTA (Experiment 1 of 3):**\n\nI will now submit my first experiment under Stagnation Protocol I. This involves integrating BAFW into my `log1p`-based SOTA replication.\nSpecifically, I will modify the `wv_graph` calculation in the SOTA module. Instead of directly `np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_g)`, I will:\n1.  Calculate `w_bafw` using `_batch_aware_feature_weights` from my local `praxis_core.py` (which I just read, so I will embed it into my submission).\n2.  Combine this `w_bafw` multiplicatively with the existing variance-based `wv_graph` (or replace it). Aletheia's code suggests applying `w_bafw` multiplicatively to the *already variance-weighted* `Xd`, so `Xw_graph = (Xw_var_scaled * w_bafw[None, :])`. I will follow this multiplicative approach.\n3.  I will use `bafw_beta=0.50` as per Aletheia I's successful submission.\n4.  All other parameters for the `log1p`-based SOTA will remain at their default values (e.g., `alpha_g=0.5`,\
    \ `n_pcs_graph=50`, `lambda` auto-selected, `k_total=48`, `kd=20`, `delta=0.10`).\n\nThis experiment aims to enhance feature weighting to better preserve biological signal and improve batch mixing, directly targeting `ASW_batch`, `ASW_label`, and `Cell_cycle`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with BAFW (log1p, beta=0.50) - Idea 1\"\ntags: \"batch integration, sota, fwpca, daqb, log1p, bafw, novel, stagnation-protocol-i\"\nabstract: \"This submission implements the first idea under Stagnation Protocol I: integrating Batch-Aware Feature Weighting (BAFW) into the log1p-based SOTA MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline. BAFW is applied multiplicatively to the variance-weighted HVG expression matrix on the graph path, using `bafw_beta=0.50`. This novel modification aims to enhance feature weighting by prioritizing genes less influenced by batch effects, thereby improving ASW_batch, ASW_label, and Cell_cycle metrics without sacrificing overall performance, building upon\
    \ the established robust baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from sklearn.decomposition import PCA # For pca_array_custom (embedded from praxis_core.py)\n\n  # Optional import for Auto-λ v2 mean-target selection\n  try:\n      from shared.diagnostics.lam_autoselect2 import autoselect_lambda_mean_target\n  except Exception:\n      # Fallback shim: fixed λ if import unavailable\n      def autoselect_lambda_mean_target(R2, gamma_max=0.74, target_mean=0.04, **_):\n          return 0.60\n\n  # ------------ Core utilities (adapted from Aletheia I's praxis_core.py and SOTA module) ------------\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\
    \n  def _pca_on_dense(Xd: np.ndarray, n_comps: int, random_state: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(np.float32)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\
    \      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      Xd_dense_for_var = Xd.A if sp.issparse(Xd) else Xd\n      var_g = Xd_dense_for_var.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return w # Return weights, not scaled Xd\n\n  def _batch_aware_feature_weights(Xd: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3, beta: float = 0.50):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((Xd.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=np.float32)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(np.float32)\n\n      if sp.issparse(Xd):\n          Xd_dense = Xd.toarray()\n      else:\n          Xd_dense = Xd\n\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Xd_dense)\n      Zhat = B @ W\n\n      var_total = Xd_dense.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      w_bafw = np.power(1.0 - R2 + 1e-8, beta).astype(np.float32)\n      return w_bafw, R2 # Returns BAFW weights and R2_g\n\n  # ------------ DAQB (density-adaptive quotas with column balancing) ------------\n  def _build_daqb(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                  delta=0.10, k_density=20, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      \"\"\"\n      Density-adaptive quota-balanced graph on Zcorr:\n        - f_cross per cell from distance to k_density-th NN across all batches.\n        - Even per-batch quotas with remainder to closest batches.\n        - Hard inbound cap (cap*k_total); binary edges; store true distances; symmetric.\n      \"\"\"\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(rng_seed)\n      Z = np.asarray(Zcorr, dtype=np.float32, order='C')\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n\
    \      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats)\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n      L, U = 0.60, 0.90\n\n      # All-batch density proxy\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * delta, L, U)\n\n      q_cross_tot = np.rint(f_cross * k_total).astype(int)\n      q_within_tot = k_total - q_cross_tot\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      # Neighbor list sizes (upper bounds)\n      k_within_max = int(np.ceil((1.0 - L) * k_total))\n      k_cross_per_max = int(np.ceil(U * k_total / B_other))\n      k_max = max(k_within_max, k_cross_per_max) + 1  # +1 to skip self\n\n      # Fit per-batch neighbor models\n      cat2code\
    \ = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cats)}\n      codes = np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n      nn_models, train_idx = {}, {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          train_idx[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          m = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          m.fit(Z[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = m\n\n      # Precompute queries\n      dists, idx_local = {}, {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n          dists[j] = d; idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      inbound = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.int32)\n      cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = codes[i]\n          q_within = int(q_within_tot[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(q_cross_tot[i])\n          other = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n\n          # Even per-batch quotas + remainder to closest batches (by first\
    \ NN distance)\n          if q_cross_total > 0 and len(other) > 0:\n              base = q_cross_total // B_other\n              rem = q_cross_total - base * B_other\n              scores = [(j, dists[j][i][0]) for j in other]\n              scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n              q_map = {j: base for j in other}\n              for k in range(rem):\n                  q_map[scores[k % len(other)][0]] += 1\n          else:\n              q_map = {j: 0 for j in other}\n\n          # Within-batch selection (cap-first, then distance)\n          d_w = dists[bi][i]; ii_w = idx_local[bi][i]\n          start_w = 1 if d_w[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          globals_w = train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]]\n          cand_inb = inbound[globals_w]; cand_dst = d_w[start_w:]\n          order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n          taken = 0\n          for idx in order:\n              g = int(globals_w[idx])\n              if inbound[g] >= cap_thr:\n                  continue\n              rows.append(i);\
    \ cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n              inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n              if taken >= q_within: break\n          if taken < q_within:\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_w[idx])\n                  if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                      continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= q_within: break\n\n          # Cross-batch selection per other batch\n          for j in other:\n              qj = q_map[j]\n              if qj <= 0: continue\n              d_c = dists[j][i]; ii_c = idx_local[j][i]\n              globals_c = train_idx[j][ii_c]\n              cand_inb = inbound[globals_c]; cand_dst = d_c\n              order = np.lexsort((cand_dst, cand_inb))\n              taken = 0\n              for idx in order:\n                  g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                  if inbound[g]\
    \ >= cap_thr:\n                      continue\n                  rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                  inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                  if taken >= qj: break\n              if taken < qj:\n                  for idx in order:\n                      g = int(globals_c[idx])\n                      if inbound[g] < cap_thr:\n                          continue\n                      rows.append(i); cols.append(g); dvals.append(float(cand_dst[idx]))\n                      inbound[g] += 1; taken += 1\n                      if taken >= qj: break\n\n      A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n          np.array(rows, np.int32), np.array(cols, np.int32), np.array(dvals, np.float32), n\n      )\n      return A_sym.astype(np.float32), D_sym.astype(np.float32)\n\n  # ------------ Main: MPB-GraphFWPCA with log1p Normalization and BAFW ------------\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\
    \n      MPB-GraphFWPCA: Feature-weighted PCA on the graph path, then BRBG + DAQB.\n      Modified to use log1p normalization and incorporate Batch-Aware Feature Weighting (BAFW)\n      for the graph path's FWPCA step.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Config (from SOTA module)\n      alpha_emb = 0.5\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n      alpha_g = 0.5 # Reverted to optimal 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      \n      # BAFW parameter\n      bafw_beta = 0.50 # MODIFIED: New parameter for BAFW\n\n      target_mean_gamma = 0.04\n      k_total = 48\n      kd = 20\n      delta = 0.10\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      cap = 2.0\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Apply log1p Normalization\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # EtC embedding (QC only; not used for graph)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_emb).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph path: GraphFWPCA with BAFW -> PCA -> residualization (Auto-λ v2) -> DAQB\n      # 1. Base variance weighting\n      wv_graph_var = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd,\
    \ alpha=alpha_g) # Returns weights\n\n      # 2. Apply BAFW multiplicatively to the variance-weighted data\n      w_bafw, R2_g_bafw = _batch_aware_feature_weights(Xd, batches=batches, l2=l2, beta=bafw_beta)\n      \n      # Multiply variance weights by BAFW weights\n      final_wv_graph = wv_graph_var * w_bafw\n      Xw_graph = Xd * final_wv_graph # Apply final weights to Xd\n      \n      Zg = _pca_on_dense(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n      # Residualize Zg against batches with per-PC shrinkage γ_j\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n      lam = autoselect_lambda_mean_target(R2, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_mean=target_mean_gamma)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # DAQB graph\n      Cg, Dg =\
    \ _build_daqb(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                           metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=kd, cap=cap, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      # Optionally record settings used\n      adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g), lambda_selected=float(lam),\n                                         target_mean_gamma=float(target_mean_gamma),\n                                         kd=int(kd), delta=float(delta), k_total=int(k_total),\n                                         bafw_beta=float(bafw_beta)) # Record new BAFW parameter\n      return adata\n```"
