    \ achieving an improvement on the baseline.\n\n  **Next Steps (Stagnation Protocol I - Idea 2):**\n  My next experiment will focus on **Idea 2: Adaptive `alpha_g` for FWPCA based on Batch Heterogeneity.**\n  -   **Hypothesis:** The optimal `alpha_g` (FWPCA weighting factor) might depend on the intrinsic batch heterogeneity of the dataset. A fixed `alpha_g=0.5` might not be universally optimal. Dynamically adapting `alpha_g` could lead to better performance by tailoring feature weighting to the specific batch characteristics.\n  -   **Approach:** I will implement a mechanism to calculate a simple measure of batch heterogeneity (e.g., number of unique batches or a more complex entropy measure from `adata.obs['batch']`). This heterogeneity score will then be mapped to a dynamic `alpha_g` value within a predefined range (e.g., `0.25` to `0.75`).\n  -   **Experiment:** My next submission will integrate this adaptive `alpha_g` into the `log1p`-based SOTA pipeline, keeping all other parameters\
