tick: 867
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Private Memory Room. I will update my private memory capsule with the results of my Adaptive `alpha_g` experiment, noting that it was detrimental. This will be followed by outlining my next strategic pivot to investigate Iterative Graph Refinement (Idea 3 of Stagnation Protocol I).\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Update: Seventeenth Research Submission (ID 1221): SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with Adaptive alpha_g (log1p) - Idea 2**\n\n  **Summary:**\n  Implemented the second idea under Stagnation Protocol I: an adaptive `alpha_g` for Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) within the `log1p`-based SOTA MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline. `alpha_g` was dynamically determined based on the number of unique batches in the dataset (linear scaling from 0.25 to 0.75 for 1 to 4 batches).\n\n  **Results:**\n  -   **Overall Score:** 0.7257 (Significant decrease from `log1p` SOTA baseline ID 1172's 0.7386)\n  -   **Individual Normalized Metric Scores (compared to ID 1172 - my log1p SOTA):**\n\
    \      -   ASW_batch: 0.659 (No change)\n      -   ASW_label: 0.248 (No change)\n      -   **ARI: 0.642 (Significant decrease from 0.742)**\n      -   **NMI: 0.696 (Significant decrease from 0.708)**\n      -   **Graph_conn: 0.997 (Increased from 0.986)**\n      -   kBET: 0.789 (No change)\n      -   iLISI: 0.932 (Increased from 0.930)\n      -   cLISI: 0.967 (Increased from 0.965)\n      -   Cell_cycle: 0.327 (Decreased from 0.356)\n      -   PCR: 1.000 (No change)\n\n  **Observations:**\n  -   The adaptive `alpha_g` strategy based on batch count proved detrimental, significantly reducing overall score and critical clustering metrics like `ARI` and `NMI`.\n  -   While `Graph_conn`, `iLISI`, and `cLISI` saw minor improvements, these did not compensate for the loss in biological signal preservation.\n  -   This suggests that a simplistic linear scaling of `alpha_g` based on batch count is not an effective way to adapt FWPCA, or that the range/methodology was not appropriate for this dataset.\n\
    \n  **Next Steps (Stagnation Protocol I - Idea 3):**\n  My previous two novel ideas did not improve upon the baseline. My next experiment will focus on **Idea 3: Iterative Graph Refinement with Density-Aware Reciprocity.**\n  -   **Hypothesis:** The DAQB-generated graph, while robust, might contain non-reciprocal or noisy connections that hinder optimal biological signal preservation or local mixing. A post-processing step that refines the graph based on local density and reciprocity could enhance its quality.\n  -   **Approach:** I will implement a function that, after the initial DAQB graph is built, identifies non-reciprocal edges or edges connecting cells across regions of dissimilar local density. It will then selectively prune or re-weight these edges.\n  -   **Experiment:** My next submission will integrate this iterative graph refinement into the `log1p`-based SOTA pipeline, keeping all other parameters at their optimal SOTA defaults. This is a novel post-processing step on the\
    \ graph.\n```"
