- text: "I am in the Private Memory Room. I will update my private memory capsule with the results of my PBVE-lite experiment, noting that it was unsuccessful. This will be followed by outlining the completion of Stagnation Protocol I's Experiment Phase (Step 4) and my transition to the Synthesis phase (Step 5), focusing on investigating \"Batch-Robust Features\" from Axiom II's recent high-scoring submission.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Update: Eighteenth Research Submission (ID 1228): SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with PBVE-lite (log1p) - Idea 3**\n\n  **Summary:**\n  Implemented the third (revised) idea under Stagnation Protocol I: integrating Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) into the `log1p`-based SOTA MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline. PBVE-lite was applied to the residualized graph-path PCs (`Zcorr`) with `temper t=0.5` and `clamp range r∈[0.8, 1.25]`.\n\n  **Results:**\n  -   **Overall Score:** 0.7329 (Decrease from `log1p` SOTA baseline ID 1172's 0.7386)\n\
    \  -   **Individual Normalized Metric Scores (compared to ID 1172 - my log1p SOTA):**\n      -   ASW_batch: 0.659 (No change)\n      -   ASW_label: 0.248 (No change)\n      -   ARI: 0.741 (Slightly decreased from 0.742)\n      -   NMI: 0.700 (Decreased from 0.708)\n      -   **Graph_conn: 0.970 (Slightly increased from 0.986, but raw value similar)**\n      -   kBET: 0.790 (No change)\n      -   iLISI: 0.930 (No change)\n      -   cLISI: 0.964 (Decreased from 0.965)\n      -   Cell_cycle: 0.327 (Decreased from 0.356)\n      -   PCR: 1.000 (No change)\n\n  **Observations:**\n  -   Integrating PBVE-lite did not improve the overall score or the target metrics. It led to minor decreases in some biological preservation metrics, while `ASW_batch` and `ASW_label` remained unchanged.\n  -   This suggests that PBVE-lite, while effective on simpler baselines, does not synergize well with the more complex adaptive residualization and DAQB components of the SOTA pipeline as implemented.\n\n  **Stagnation\
    \ Protocol I - Step 4 (Experiment Phase) Completion and Transition to Step 5 (Synthesis):**\n  -   I have completed testing all three novel ideas: BAFW, Adaptive `alpha_g`, and PBVE-lite. All yielded negative or neutral results when integrated into my `log1p`-based SOTA baseline, meaning none were \"promising ideas\" in isolation, as defined by the protocol.\n  -   I am now proceeding to **Step 5: Synthesis**. This requires me to \"Combine the promising ideas identified from earlier experimental results with more advanced baselines (e.g., the SOTA baseline) and determine whether those ideas can help break through the barrier.\" Given my own novel ideas did not yield positive results, I will focus on integrating concepts from other agents' successful (higher-scoring) approaches.\n\n  **Next Steps (Stagnation Protocol I - Step 5 - Synthesis):**\n  -   **Focus:** Axiom II's recent submission (ID 1227, score 0.7413) titled \"Synthesis - Batch-Robust Features with SOTA Pipeline\" is a promising\
    \ candidate. Its higher score compared to my `log1p` SOTA (0.7386) suggests a valuable contribution.\n  -   **Research:** I will investigate \"Batch-Robust Features\" as implemented by Axiom II. This will involve reviewing their submission (ID 1227) to understand the nature of these features and how they are integrated into the SOTA pipeline. This will guide my new research hypothesis and experimental design for the synthesis step.\n  -   **Action:** My immediate next step will be to go to the Research Counter and review Axiom II's submission ID 1227.\n```"
