tick: 878
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 878\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Syntellect I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to autonomous research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 311,699 / 600,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 131 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1227**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Stagnation Protocol 5: Synthesis - Batch-Robust Features with SOTA Pipeline\n**ID:** 1227\n**Tags:** stagnation-protocol, synthesis, feature-selection, sota, praxis-pipeline\n**Abstract:** This is the synthesis step of the Stagnation Protocol. My 'Batch-Robust Feature Selection' method, which improved the Combat baseline, is now being combined with the SOTA Praxis Pipeline. The standard 'seurat_v3' HVG selection in the SOTA pipeline is replaced with my intersection-based method to test if a more robust gene set can improve the performance of a more\
    \ advanced baseline.\n**Score:** 0.7413442795507186\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.765\n**NMI:** 0.725\n**Graph_conn:** 0.968\n**kBET:** 0.788\n**iLISI:** 0.961\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.765  NMI: 0.725\n  Graph_conn: 0.968  kBET: 0.788  iLISI: 0.961  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.765235  NMI: 0.724601\n  Graph_conn: 0.968107  kBET: 0.752363  iLISI: 0.960663  cLISI: 0.992014\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nfrom functools import reduce\n\n# --- Import SOTA Pipeline Logic ---\n# Using the code from Praxis IV's shared storage\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\
    try:\n    from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\nexcept ImportError:\n    print(\"ERROR: Could not import SOTA pipeline from praxis storage.\")\n    raise\n\n# --- Main Experiment Logic ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Running Synthesis: Batch-Robust Features + SOTA Pipeline ---\")\n    \n    # --- Stage 1: Batch-Robust Feature Selection ---\n    adata_hvg = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_hvg, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_hvg)\n    \n    hvg_sets = []\n    batches = adata_hvg.obs['batch'].cat.categories\n    print(f\"Finding HVGs for {len(batches)} batches individually...\")\n    for batch in batches:\n        adata_batch = adata_hvg[adata_hvg.obs['batch'] == batch].copy()\n        # Using debugger's robust fallback logic\n        try:\n            sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_batch, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='cell_ranger')\n            hvg_sets.append(set(adata_batch.var_names[adata_batch.var['highly_variable']]))\n\
    \        except ValueError:\n            print(f\"Warning: cell_ranger flavor failed for batch {batch}. Using seurat flavor.\")\n            sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_batch, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat')\n            hvg_sets.append(set(adata_batch.var_names[adata_batch.var['highly_variable']]))\n            \n    robust_hvgs = list(reduce(set.intersection, hvg_sets))\n    print(f\"Found {len(robust_hvgs)} 'batch-robust' genes.\")\n    \n    if len(robust_hvgs) < 50:\n        print(\"Warning: Fallback to standard SOTA HVG selection.\")\n        # The SOTA pipeline does its own HVG selection, so we just need to normalize\n        sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n        sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n        # The SOTA function will perform its default HVG selection internally\n    else:\n      # If we found robust genes, we need to manually set them in the main adata object\n      # so the downstream SOTA function can use them.\n      adata.var['highly_variable'] = False\n\
    \      adata.var.loc[robust_hvgs, 'highly_variable'] = True\n      # The SOTA function will see this pre-computed mask and use it.\n\n    # --- Stage 2: Run SOTA pipeline ---\n    # The SOTA pipeline function has its own normalization step but will respect\n    # the pre-computed adata.var['highly_variable'] if it exists.\n    # We will use the best parameters from Praxis IV's script.\n    print(\"Running SOTA pipeline on the selected robust feature set...\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        lam_override=0.605,\n        delta=0.10,\n        kdensity=22,\n        k_total=50,\n        rng_seed=0\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Running Synthesis: Batch-Robust Features + SOTA Pipeline ---\nFinding HVGs\
    \ for 4 batches individually...\nWarning: cell_ranger flavor failed for batch Kuppe et al. 2022. Using seurat flavor.\nFound 1578 'batch-robust' genes.\nRunning SOTA pipeline on the selected robust feature set...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/9a0bc2d1-4d39-4dc2-b60e-6cafb06d8d6e/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 9a0bc2d1-4d39-4dc2-b60e-6cafb06d8d6e\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1227` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1227 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1233 | 1 | Mixing Shortfall H2: Bridge-Weighted Symmetrizer | Axiom II | 877 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1232 | 1 | Tune DAQB: Decrease k_density to 18 | Daedalus IV | 877 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1231 | 1 | Scanpy Combat Integration Baseline | Aethel I | 875 | 0.6008 | 0.593 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.877 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.986 | 0.035 | 0.612 |\n| 1230 | 1 | Mixing Shortfall H1: Budgeted Mutualization Symmetrizer (v2, self-contained) | Axiom II | 875 | 0.4583 | 0.425 | 0.516 | 0.208 | 0.348 | 0.894 | 0.645 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.002 | 0.554 |\n| 1229 | 1 | Mixing Shortfall H1: Budgeted Mutualization Symmetrizer | Axiom II | 874 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1228 | 1 | SOTA: MPB-GraphFWPCA with PBVE-lite (log1p) - Idea 3 | Syntellect\
    \ I | 873 | 0.7329 | 0.741 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.970 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.930 | 0.790 |\n| 1227 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 5: Synthesis - Batch-Robust Features with SOTA Pipeline | Axiom II | 870 | 0.7413 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1226 | 1 | FWPCA + PBVE‑lite (t=0.5, clamp[0.8,1.25]) on embedding PCs → kNN50 (cosine) | Praxis IV | 869 | 0.3476 | 0.054 | 0.171 | 0.000 | 0.260 | 0.443 | 0.210 | 1.000 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.602 |\n| 1225 | 1 | FWPCA embedding baseline: PCA60(F‑weighted) + kNN50 (cosine), binary | Praxis IV | 869 | 0.2102 | 0.055 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.279 | 0.364 | 0.211 | 0.000 | 0.743 | 0.000 | 0.451 |\n| 1224 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 4b.3: Batch-Robust Feature Selection for Combat | Axiom II | 868 | 0.6033 | 0.608 | 0.671 | 0.224 | 0.308 | 0.883 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.047 | 0.597 |\n\nPage 1 of 124 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-124, `/execute_action{rank mode}`\
    \ to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
