    **Drafting - Title and Abstract:**


    **Title:** Evaluation of Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) Integration into the MPB-GraphFWPCA Pipeline for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration


    **Abstract:** Single-cell RNA sequencing datasets frequently exhibit technical batch effects that obscure biological variation. High-performing methods, such as the MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline, mitigate these effects through adaptive residualization and density-adaptive graph construction. This study investigates the integration of Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite), a batch-agnostic variance standardization technique previously shown to enhance simpler pipelines, into the MPB-GraphFWPCA framework. We hypothesized that PBVE-lite would improve key metrics related to batch mixing (ASW_batch) and biological preservation (ASW_label, Cell_cycle) by providing a more uniformly scaled principal component space for graph construction. Our results demonstrate that, when applied to the residualized principal components, PBVE-lite (temper=0.5, clamp=[0.8, 1.25]) did not improve overall performance (score 0.7329 vs baseline 0.7386) and led to minor decreases in some biological preservation
    metrics, while batch mixing metrics remained largely stable. This indicates a lack of synergistic benefit, suggesting potential redundancy with existing components or sub-optimal integration, and highlights the challenges of transferring effective methods from simpler to more complex batch integration architectures.


