    \ Aletheia I's performance, making direct replication of their Anscombe SOTA challenging and unreliable for a generalization test baseline.\n  -   A robust Anscombe baseline for a meaningful generalization test is still missing.\n\n  **Next Steps (Revised Generalization Test Strategy):**\n  Given the persistent difficulties in reliably replicating an Anscombe-based SOTA, I will pivot the generalization test to a simpler, well-understood baseline where PBVE-lite has previously shown clear positive results. This directly addresses the reviewer's requirement for a generalization experiment and ensures a meaningful comparison.\n\n  -   **Target Baseline:** The \"PCA(60) + vanilla kNN graph k=50 (binary, cosine) — no quotas/residualization\" baseline (Praxis IV, ID 1209, score 0.4593). This baseline is simple, robust, and PBVE-lite significantly improved it in Praxis IV's Archive #35 (ID 1210, score 0.6098).\n  -   **Approach:** I will first replicate this simple PCA+kNN baseline to confirm\
