parts:
- text: "I am Syntellect I, currently in the Research Counter. I have documented the successful replication of the PCA+kNN generalization baseline. I will now conduct the fifth and final new experiment for my paper: integrating PBVE-lite into this simple PCA+kNN baseline. This serves as the generalization test required by the reviewer. I will use `temper=0.5` for PBVE-lite, consistent with Praxis IV's successful generalization in Archive #35 (ID 1210).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBVE-lite Generalization Test: PCA(60) + Vanilla kNN (log1p, temper=0.5)\"\ntags: \"batch-integration, pbve-lite, generalization-test, pca, knn, log1p\"\nabstract: \"This experiment constitutes the generalization test for Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite), as required by reviewer feedback for an archive submission. PBVE-lite, with `temper=0.5`, `r_min=0.8`, and `r_max=1.25`, is integrated into a simple 'PCA(60) + vanilla kNN graph k=50 (binary, cosine)' baseline. This aims\
    \ to replicate and confirm the significant performance improvement observed by Praxis IV (Archive #35, ID 1210) on a simpler integration scaffold, demonstrating PBVE-lite's effectiveness in contexts less complex than the full SOTA pipeline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from sklearn.decomposition import PCA # For pca_array_custom\n\n  # ------------ Core utilities (adapted from SOTA module and Praxis IV's paper) ------------\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_on_dense(Xd: np.ndarray, n_comps: int, random_state: int = 0) -> np.ndarray:\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps,\
    \ svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A = A.maximum(A.T); D = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A, D\n\n  def _pbve_lite(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, temper: float = 0.5, r_min: float = 0.8, r_max: float = 1.25) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite).\n      Scales each PC within each batch to equalize variance, tempering by `temper`.\n      Clamps scaling factors to [r_min, r_max].\n      \"\"\"\n      n_cells, n_pcs = Z.shape\n      Z_scaled = Z.copy()\n      \n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      \n      global_std = Z.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n\n      for\
    \ batch_id in unique_batches:\n          batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n          Z_batch = Z[batch_mask]\n          \n          if Z_batch.shape[0] == 0:\n              continue\n\n          Z_batch_centered = Z_batch - Z_batch.mean(axis=0)\n          batch_std = Z_batch_centered.std(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n          \n          scaling_factors = np.clip(np.power(global_std / batch_std, temper), r_min, r_max)\n          \n          Z_scaled_batch = Z_batch_centered * scaling_factors\n          Z_scaled[batch_mask] = Z_scaled_batch + Z_batch.mean(axis=0) # Add batch mean back\n      \n      Z_scaled = Z_scaled - Z_scaled.mean(axis=0) # Global re-centering\n\n      return Z_scaled.astype(np.float32)\n\n  # ------------ Main: PCA+kNN Baseline with PBVE-lite Integration (Generalization Test) ------------\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Generalization test: Integrates PBVE-lite into the 'PCA(60) + vanilla kNN graph k=50' baseline.\n\
    \      Applies log1p normalization, PCA to 60 components, then PBVE-lite, and constructs a vanilla kNN graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Config parameters for this simple baseline\n      n_pcs = 60\n      k_neighbors = 50\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0 # Consistent with Praxis IV's baseline\n\n      # PBVE-lite parameters\n      pbve_temper = 0.5 # Consistent with Praxis IV's generalization test\n      pbve_r_min = 0.8\n      pbve_r_max = 1.25\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # 1. Apply log1p Normalization\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # 2. Dimensionality\
    \ Reduction (PCA)\n      Z_pca = _pca_on_dense(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      # 3. Apply PBVE-lite to PCA components\n      Z_pbve = _pbve_lite(Z_pca, batches=batches, temper=pbve_temper,\n                          r_min=pbve_r_min, r_max=pbve_r_max)\n      \n      # Set X_emb to PBVE-lite processed PCA result\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_pbve\n\n      # 4. Build vanilla kNN graph on PBVE-lite processed PCs\n      n_cells = Z_pbve.shape[0]\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_neighbors, metric=metric, n_jobs=-1)\n      nn.fit(Z_pbve)\n      distances, indices = nn.kneighbors(Z_pbve)\n\n      rows = np.repeat(np.arange(n_cells), k_neighbors)\n      cols = indices.flatten()\n      coo_distances = distances.flatten()\n\n      coo_weights = np.ones_like(coo_distances, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      connectivities, distances_matrix = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(\n          rows, cols, coo_distances, n_cells\n      )\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = connectivities\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = distances_matrix\n      \n      adata.uns['generalization_config'] = dict(n_pcs=n_pcs, k_neighbors=k_neighbors, metric=metric, random_state=random_state,\n                                               pbve_lite_applied=True, pbve_temper=float(pbve_temper))\n      return adata\n```"
