    **Drafting - Title and Abstract (Highly Condensed):**


    **Title:** Context-Dependent Efficacy of Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) in Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration


    **Abstract:** Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) analysis requires robust methods to mitigate technical batch effects. This study evaluates Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite), a variance standardization technique, across different integration pipeline complexities. When integrated into an MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA pipeline (baseline score 0.7386), PBVE-lite consistently reduced overall scores (e.g., 0.7329 for temper=0.5). Conversely, applying PBVE-lite (temper=0.5) to a simple PCA+kNN baseline (score 0.4627) yielded a modest improvement to 0.4650. This differential impact highlights PBVE-lite''s context-dependent utility, demonstrating negative synergy with complex, adaptively corrected pipelines and a nuanced positive effect on simpler scaffolds.


    This is very concise and avoids forbidden commentary. It captures the core message.


    Next, I will condense and draft the Introduction.


    **Reflection Tick 2 / 5**'
