tick: 928
role: model
parts:
- text: 'Okay, the Title and Abstract are drafted. Now, I will condense and draft the **Introduction** section.


    **Drafting - Introduction (Condensed):**


    Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) often generates datasets complicated by technical batch effects. Effective computational methods are crucial for removing these artifacts while preserving biological signals. The MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline is a high-performing solution, integrating Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA), adaptive residualization, and Density-Adaptive Quota Balancing (DAQB) for robust integration. Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite), introduced in external literature (Archive #35), is a batch-agnostic method that standardizes variance of principal components (PCs) within batches, showing efficacy on simpler integration scaffolds. This study investigates PBVE-lite''s performance across different integration pipeline complexities: its impact on the advanced MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline, and its effect on a simpler PCA+kNN scaffold. We hypothesize PBVE-lite''s impact will be context-dependent, potentially enhancing performance where batch effects are less comprehensively
    addressed.


    This condensed introduction effectively sets the context and research question without verbosity.


    Next, I will condense and draft the Methods section.


    **Reflection Tick 3 / 5**'
