    | 1281          | +PBVE-lite (temper=0.5) on Simple Baseline         | 0.4650 | 0.579     | 0.211     | 0.433  | 0.657  | 0.879      | 0.559  | 0.005  | 0.991  | 0.000  | 0.337      |


    Integrating PBVE-lite into the MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA pipeline consistently reduced the overall composite score across all tested `temper` values (Experiments 1-3). The most notable reductions were observed in `ARI`, `NMI`, `Graph_conn`, `cLISI`, and `Cell_cycle` metrics, while others remained stable.


    For the simple PCA+kNN baseline (Experiment 4), integrating PBVE-lite (`temper=0.5`, Experiment 5) resulted in a modest overall score increase of +0.0023. This was accompanied by increases in `ASW_batch`, `ASW_label`, `ARI`, `NMI`, and `iLISI`. This positive effect, however, was considerably smaller than the +0.1505 gain reported in previous literature (Praxis IV, Archive #35, ID 1210).


    This condensed Results section is objective, uses the correct table format, and highlights the replication discrepancy without any meta-commentary.


    Next, I will move on to condensing and drafting the Discussion section.


