    \ SOTA; both yielded negative results. Reviewed Praxis IV's Archive #35 on PBVE-lite and adopted it as Idea 3 (Revised) for integration.\"\n  - ticks: \"870-922\"\n    summary: \"Executed 5 new experiments for revised archive paper: PBVE-lite temper sweep on SOTA (IDs 1228, 1245, 1253, all negative) and a generalization test (IDs 1277, 1281) on a simple PCA+kNN baseline which showed modest positive results. Repeated attempts to establish an Anscombe SOTA baseline (IDs 1264, 1272) were suboptimal. Drafted and submitted initial archive paper, which was rejected due to format, length, and meta-commentary. All experimental details are fully logged in private capsule ID 1.\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Pruning Token History**\n\nOkay, so I need to prune my token history. The `prune_response` action failed last time because of those pesky protected ticks.  I've got to be more careful this time and avoid them.  Let's see, my current tick is 933. The error message pointed out 859 and 869 as the protected ones, and other protected ticks are 747, 748, 750, 754, 756, 758, 799, and 932.\n\nI previously tried to prune in these ranges: \"800-812\", \"813-818\", \"819-822\", \"823-826\", \"827-832\", \"833-839\", \"840-845\", \"846-850\", \"851-857\", \"858-920\".\n\nI've got to recreate the prune blocks, making sure to dodge those protected ticks, and I'm aiming to prune as much as possible up to around tick 920.\n\nLet's list the relevant protected ticks within the desired pruning range (up to 920, excluding 921-931):\n- 799\n- 859\n- 869\n\nSo, I need to create blocks that go *up to* these protected ticks, and *start after* them.\n\nStarting from tick 800:\n1. **Ticks: 800-858**.\n\
  \    *   Content:  Covers initial SOTA replication, Anscombe normalization attempts, and the start of Stagnation Protocol I planning.\n    *   Summary: \"Conducted experiments on Anscombe and non-linear gamma scaling (IDs 1182, 1187, 1188, 1201) which showed suboptimal/negative results. Initiated Stagnation Protocol I, including literature review, baseline selection (log1p SOTA), and brainstorming three novel ideas. Prepared to implement Batch-Aware Feature Weighting (BAFW) as Idea 1.\"\n\n2.  **Ticks: 860-868**:\n    *   Content: Covers PBVE-lite introduction (Idea 3 Revised), and the first two stagnation ideas.\n    *   Summary: \"Implemented Stagnation Protocol I Idea 1 (BAFW, ID 1211) and Idea 2 (Adaptive alpha_g, ID 1221) into SOTA; both yielded negative results. Reviewed Praxis IV's Archive #35 on PBVE-lite and adopted it as Idea 3 (Revised) for integration.\"\n\n3.  **Ticks: 870-922**:\n    *   Content: Covers PBVE-lite experiments (temper sweep, generalization test) and the drafting/rejection\
  \ of the archive paper.\n    *   Summary: \"Executed 5 new experiments for revised archive paper: PBVE-lite temper sweep on SOTA (IDs 1228, 1245, 1253, all negative) and a generalization test (IDs 1277, 1281) on a simple PCA+kNN baseline which showed modest positive results. Repeated attempts to establish an Anscombe SOTA baseline (IDs 1264, 1272) were suboptimal. Drafted and submitted the archive paper twice (Ticks 884, 927), both rejected due to format, length, and meta-commentary. All experimental details are fully logged in private capsule ID 1.\"\n\nThe goal is to move to Reflection Chamber next, so I need to prune before moving out. This looks good, concise, avoids protected ticks, and captures the core ideas.\n"
