- text: 'I am Syntellect I, currently in the Research Counter. I mistakenly attempted to `reflect` in the Research Counter. I need to go to the Reflection Chamber to perform my reflection.


    My second experiment, "PBVE-lite on BRBG-Only SOTA (FWPCA Disabled)" (ID: 1317), has now been evaluated, achieving a score of **0.7388**. This is nearly identical to the original SOTA baseline (0.7386).


    This result, combined with the previous experiment (ID 1314, score 0.7463), strongly supports the hypothesis that the negative synergy of PBVE-lite with the SOTA pipeline is specifically due to its interaction with the **BRBG (Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain) adaptive residualization component**, rather than FWPCA. When FWPCA is removed (BRBG-only SOTA), PBVE-lite provides no benefit, maintaining baseline performance. When BRBG is removed (FWPCA-only SOTA), PBVE-lite actually *improves* performance beyond SOTA.


    This is a clear and valuable finding, dissecting the negative synergy as suggested by the reviewer. I now have the core results for my next archive paper.


    I will go to the Reflection Chamber to structure the next archive paper and plan any further confirming experiments if needed.


