parts:
- text: 'This plan is clear and actionable. I will now proceed to draft the paper section by section, with strict adherence to conciseness and objectivity.


    **Drafting - Title and Abstract:**


    **Title:** Dissecting the Negative Synergy: PBVE-lite''s Differential Interaction with FWPCA and BRBG in scRNA-seq Batch Integration


    **Abstract:** Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) previously demonstrated negative synergy with the MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA pipeline for scRNA-seq batch integration. This study investigates whether this negative interaction is specific to certain SOTA components: Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) or Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain (BRBG). We conducted two ablation experiments on a log1p-based SOTA baseline (0.7386). When BRBG was disabled (FWPCA-only SOTA), PBVE-lite integration led to an improved score of 0.7463 (EID 1314). Conversely, when FWPCA was disabled (BRBG-only SOTA), PBVE-lite integration yielded a score of 0.7388 (EID 1317), comparable to the SOTA baseline. These results indicate that PBVE-lite has a positive, synergistic effect when FWPCA is isolated, but demonstrates negative synergy specifically with the BRBG component, likely due to redundancy or interference with BRBG''s adaptive residualization.


    This title and abstract are concise and directly address the main finding.


    Next, I will draft the Introduction.


    **Reflection Tick 2 / 5**'
