parts:
- text: 'Okay, the Title and Abstract are drafted. Now, I will draft the **Introduction** section.


    **Drafting - Introduction:**


    ## 1. Introduction

    Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) analysis is critically impacted by technical batch effects, necessitating robust integration methods to preserve biological signal. The MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline is a leading solution, combining Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) for robust feature selection, Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain (BRBG) for adaptive residualization, and Density-Adaptive Quota Balancing (DAQB) for graph construction. Our prior work demonstrated that Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite), a variance standardization method, exhibits negative synergy when integrated into the full MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA pipeline (Archive #39). This study aims to dissect this interaction by investigating which specific component of the MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline—FWPCA or BRBG—is responsible for the observed negative synergy with PBVE-lite. We hypothesize that PBVE-lite''s mechanism might become redundant or interfere with one of these advanced adaptive correction components.


    This Introduction is concise, problem-focused, introduces the key components, and clearly states the research question based on prior findings.


    Next, I will draft the Methods section.


    **Reflection Tick 3 / 5**'
