- text: "Okay, the Introduction is drafted. Now, I will draft the **Methods** section, focusing on conciseness and clear referencing of EIDs and modifications.\n\n**Drafting - Methods:**\n\n## 2. Methods\n\n**2.1 Dataset and Preprocessing**\nThe Human Heart Dataset (~20,000 cells, 2,000 highly variable genes (HVGs)) was used. Raw UMI counts were normalized (10,000/cell), log1p transformed, and HVGs selected (`seurat_v3` flavor, `n_top_genes=2000`).\n\n**2.2 Baseline and Experimental Modifications**\n*   **SOTA Baseline:** The `log1p`-based MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline (EID 1172, score 0.7386) served as the foundation. Full parameter details for this pipeline are available in Evaluation ID 1172.\n*   **PBVE-lite Integration:** PBVE-lite (`temper=0.5`, clamped `[r_min=0.8, r_max=1.25]`) was integrated by applying its variance standardization to the principal components after PCA and BRBG residualization (`Zcorr`), immediately prior to DAQB graph construction.\n*   **Experiment 1: PBVE-lite on FWPCA-Only\
    \ SOTA (BRBG Disabled) (EID 1314)**\n    BRBG was disabled in the SOTA pipeline by setting `gamma_max = 0.0` and `lam_override = 0.0`. PBVE-lite was then applied.\n*   **Experiment 2: PBVE-lite on BRBG-Only SOTA (FWPCA Disabled) (EID 1317)**\n    FWPCA was disabled by setting `alpha_emb = 0.0` and `alpha_g = 0.0`. BRBG remained active. PBVE-lite was then applied.\n\n**2.3 Evaluation Protocol**\nExperiments used evaluator v4.1. Performance was assessed using OpenProblems 2.0 metrics (ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle), with a composite score (arithmetic mean). EIDs are provided for reproducibility.\n\nThis Methods section is highly condensed, citing EIDs for full baseline parameters and clearly explaining how FWPCA/BRBG were disabled.\n\nNext, I will draft the Results section.\n\n**Reflection Tick 4 / 5**"
