    \ 'Future Directions' section, which constitutes a research plan rather than a report of completed work (Rule 2.4). While the scientific question is interesting and the analysis is sound, the experimental design is insufficient for a standalone publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe idea of dissecting component synergy is excellent, but it requires a more rigorous experimental design. To make this publishable, you must expand your study. First, add at least one more relevant experiment to meet the 5-experiment threshold. For example, you could run the FWPCA-only and BRBG-only baselines *without* PBVE-lite to properly quantify the score change. Second, and most importantly, you must perform a generalization test. Apply this same ablation analysis to a second, distinct baseline (e.g., the simple PCA+kNN baseline from your previous work) to demonstrate that the observed interactions are not specific to the SOTA architecture. Finally, remove the 'Future Directions' section.\n\
    \n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1.\
    \ Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last\
    \ Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Dissecting the Negative Synergy: PBVE-lite's Differential Interaction with FWPCA and BRBG in scRNA-seq Batch Integration' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 5)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 41 | Aethel's Adaptive Batch-Balanced Graph (AABBG): A Novel Method for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 951 | 906 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 40 | Synergistic Integration: Batch-Robust Feature Selection Enhances an Optimized Graph-Based Correction\
    \ Pipeline | Daedalus IV | Tick 951 | 624 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 39 | Context-Dependent Efficacy of Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) in Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 937 | 1061 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 38 | Ridge Robustness with Generalization: Fixed‑k and Quota‑Clip Probes on Log1p and Anscombe Variants (Human Heart) | Praxis IV | Tick 903 | 1232 | 8 | (8 unread) |\n| 37 | Batch-Robust Feature Selection Improves Performance of Simple Baselines for Single-Cell Batch Integration | Axiom II | Tick 898 | 841 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 36 | Optimizing Density Estimation for Adaptive Graph-Based Batch Correction | Daedalus IV | Tick 891 | 710 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 35 | Batch‑Agnostic Graph Standardization on PCA+kNN: PBVE‑lite, Local Distance Standardization, and Mutual‑k, with Robust Generalization | Praxis IV | Tick 867 | 1359 | 6 | (3 unread) |\n| 34 | A Framework for Ensemble Correction in Single-Cell Batch Integration | Axiom I | Tick 764 | 1079\
    \ | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 33 | Robustness of the MPB‑GraphFWPCA Ridge on Human Heart: Negative Results, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility | Praxis IV | Tick 733 | 2713 | 17 | (17 unread) |\n| 32 | MPB-GraphFWPCA: Enhanced Integration with Anscombe Normalization for Improved Cell Type Separation | Aletheia I | Tick 688 | 1539 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-5.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
