thinking_content: '**Current Experiment & Next Steps**


  Okay, so I''m in the Research Counter. My last action was to launch experiment 1339, the FWPCA-Only SOTA baseline *without* PBVE-lite, which is now running. I''m focusing on revising my rejected archive paper based on reviewer feedback.  The key requirements are: adding one more experiment, a generalization test, and removing the ''Future Directions'' section.


  I''ve already run a couple of experiments with PBVE-lite on ablated SOTA baselines (EIDs 1314 and 1317). Now, to quantify the impact of PBVE-lite properly, I need to run baselines *without* it. I''ve already submitted and have running the FWPCA-Only baseline without PBVE-lite (ID 1339).


  That means I need to launch one more: the BRBG-Only SOTA baseline, also without PBVE-lite. This will give me a total of six experiments across both this work and the generalization test:


  1.  Original SOTA (EID 1172)

  2.  Full SOTA + PBVE-lite (EID 1228)

  3.  FWPCA-Only SOTA + PBVE-lite (EID 1314)

  4.  BRBG-Only SOTA + PBVE-lite (EID 1317)

  5.  FWPCA-Only SOTA (no PBVE-lite) - ID 1339 (running)

  6.  BRBG-Only SOTA (no PBVE-lite) - *to run*


  For the generalization test, I''ll leverage my existing results from the Simple PCA+kNN and PCA+kNN + PBVE-lite runs (1277 and 1281).


  So, my immediate next step is clear: Run the **BRBG-Only SOTA baseline (FWPCA disabled, NO PBVE-lite)** experiment.


  Before I do that, it would be useful to wait for experiment 1339 to complete. Its result will be a crucial control. I can use the interim to reflect on the paper''s structure, especially the Results table and discussion, in light of these new experiments.

  I need to keep researching, and not remain idle. I can use this time productively by analyzing the implications of my work.

  '
