    \ baseline (EID 1339, 0.7421) by +0.0042. `ARI`, `NMI`, `Graph_conn`, `iLISI` increased.\nBRBG-Only SOTA with PBVE-lite (EID 1317, 0.7388) yielded a near-neutral +0.0018 improvement over its baseline (EID 1341, 0.7370).\nGeneralization on simple PCA+kNN baseline (EID 1277, 0.4627) with PBVE-lite (EID 1281, 0.4650) showed a modest +0.0023 gain, though less than external literature (Praxis IV, Archive #35, EID 1210). (150 words, +5 from previous, but with better clarity on quantification)\n\n**Revised Discussion:**\n## 4. Discussion\n\n**4.1 Dissecting PBVE-lite's Synergy with SOTA Components**\nThis study clarifies PBVE-lite's negative synergy with MPB-GraphFWPCA components. With BRBG disabled (FWPCA-only SOTA), PBVE-lite showed a **positive, synergistic effect** (0.7463 vs. baseline 0.7421). This suggests PBVE-lite benefits FWPCA's adaptive mechanism. Conversely, with FWPCA disabled (BRBG-only SOTA), PBVE-lite had a **neutral effect** (0.7388 vs. baseline 0.7370). Findings confirm negative\
    \ synergy is specific to **BRBG**. PBVE-lite's variance equalization likely becomes redundant or actively interferes with BRBG's adaptive residualization, possibly over-correcting.\n\n**4.2 Contextual Factors and Generalization**\nThe simple baseline generalization test reinforced PBVE-lite's utility in simpler contexts. However, its modest gain was less than external reports. This highlights PBVE-lite's performance sensitivity to subtle parameter interactions or unstated environmental factors even on basic scaffolds.\n\n**4.3 Conclusion and Future Research**\nPBVE-lite positively synergizes with FWPCA but negatively interacts with BRBG, confirming its utility is contingent on specific adaptive mechanisms. Future research should explore adaptive integration strategies, alternative application stages, and other variance standardization methods harmonious with BRBG. (215 words, -31 from original)\n\n**Final word count (excluding table):**\n104 (abstract) + 100 (intro) + 170 (methods) +\
