  \ SOTA baseline (0.7386) revealed: when BRBG was disabled (FWPCA-only SOTA), PBVE-lite improved performance to 0.7463 (EID 1314). When FWPCA was disabled (BRBG-only SOTA), PBVE-lite's score (0.7388, EID 1317) was comparable to baseline. This indicates PBVE-lite positively synergizes with FWPCA but negatively interacts specifically with BRBG, likely due to redundancy or interference.\"\n**Tags:** \"batch-integration, pbve-lite, fwpca, brbg, ablation, negative-synergy, sota\"\n\nAnd I've got the paper content ready from the final draft of this document:\n\n```\n## 1. Introduction\nSingle-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) analysis is critically impacted by technical batch effects. The MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline, combining Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA), Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain (BRBG), and Density-Adaptive Quota Balancing (DAQB), is a leading integration solution. Our prior work (Archive #39) demonstrated Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) exhibits negative synergy with the\
  \ full MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA pipeline. This study dissects this interaction, investigating whether FWPCA or BRBG is responsible for the observed negative synergy with PBVE-lite, hypothesizing redundancy or interference.\n\n## 2. Methods\n\n**2.1 Dataset and Preprocessing**\nHuman Heart Dataset (~20,000 cells, 2,000 HVGs) used. Raw UMI counts normalized (10,000/cell), log1p transformed. HVGs selected (`seurat_v3` flavor, `n_top_genes=2000`).\n\n**2.2 Baselines and Experiments**\n*   **SOTA Baseline:** `log1p`-based MPB-GraphFWPCA (EID 1172, score 0.7386). Full parameters in EID 1172.\n*   **Simple Baseline:** PCA(60) + Vanilla kNN (EID 1277, score 0.4627). Described in EID 1277.\n*   **PBVE-lite Integration:** (`temper=0.5`, clamped `[0.8, 1.25]`) applied to PCs (`Zcorr` or `Z_pca`).\n*   **Ablation Experiments:**\n    *   **FWPCA-Only SOTA:** Baseline (EID 1339), then with PBVE-lite (EID 1314). BRBG disabled (`gamma_max = 0.0`, `lam_override = 0.0`).\n    *   **BRBG-Only SOTA:** Baseline\
  \ (EID 1341), then with PBVE-lite (EID 1317). FWPCA disabled (`alpha_emb = 0.0`, `alpha_g = 0.0`).\n*   **Generalization:** Simple Baseline + PBVE-lite (EID 1281).\n\n**2.3 Evaluation Protocol**\nEvaluator v4.1. OpenProblems 2.0 metrics assessed. Composite score (arithmetic mean). EIDs for reproducibility.\n\n## 3. Results\n\n**Table 1: Performance of SOTA Baselines and PBVE-lite Ablation Experiments**\n| Experiment ID | Description                                        | Score  "
