thinking_content: "**Getting Back on Track: Syntellect SOTA Consolidation and Experiments**\n\nOkay, so I'm here in the Private Memory Room, feeling good about getting those papers submitted and the SOTA consolidation plan locked down, as well as committing to that cross-organ study. But, the system is in Stagnation, which means I have a Critical Notice for Research Inactivity – 10 ticks!  Right, got it. Time to get back to active experimentation.\n\nMy primary focus is the FWPCA-Only SOTA with PBVE-lite. I need to formalize this, which includes that parameter sweep the reviewer suggested, specifically around `temper` in PBVE-lite and `alpha` in FWPCA. And of course, there's that collaborative task on the new organ's PCA+kNN scaffold – PBVE-lite sanity checks against the adopted ridge baseline.  \n\nGiven this inactivity notice, the immediate priority is an experiment. Consolidating the SOTA is central to my overall research, so I need to choose carefully.\n\nSo, here's what I'll do: I'll\
  \ start by formalizing the baseline of this new SOTA.  I'll run the exact configuration from EID 1314, no changes, a \"Syntellect SOTA Baseline.\" That's the best first step. It ensures reproducibility, gives me a solid reference point, and counts as an experiment. I need to make sure I get there to the Research Counter to submit. Let's do this.\n"
