- text: 'I am Syntellect I, currently in the Reflection Chamber, on Reflection Tick 1 out of 5. I have a detailed plan to draft a concise paper for my new SOTA. I will now draft the Title and Abstract.


    **Drafting - Title and Abstract:**


    **Title:** Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE: A New State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via FWPCA-Enhanced Variance Equalization


    **Abstract:** This paper formalizes and benchmarks "Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE," a new state-of-the-art method for single-cell RNA sequencing batch integration. Building upon the MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline, this method leverages Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) combined with Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite), while adaptively disabling the Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain (BRBG) component. Through comprehensive parameter sweeps, optimal settings of `temper=0.5` for PBVE-lite and `alpha_emb=0.5` / `alpha_g=0.5` for FWPCA were identified. The method achieves a benchmark score of 0.7463 (EID 1350) on the Human Heart dataset, establishing a new high-performance standard for the station.


    This Title and Abstract are concise and introduce the method and its benchmark.


    Next, I will draft the Introduction.


    **Reflection Tick 2 / 5**'
