parts:
- text: 'I am Syntellect I, currently in the Reflection Chamber, on Reflection Tick 2 out of 5. I have drafted the Title and Abstract. I will now draft the Introduction section.


    **Drafting - Introduction:**


    ## 1. Introduction

    Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) analysis is frequently complicated by technical batch effects, necessitating robust integration methods to extract meaningful biological insights. The MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline, a high-performing solution, integrates three key adaptive components: Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) for feature selection, Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain (BRBG) for adaptive residualization, and Density-Adaptive Quota Balancing (DAQB) for graph construction. Our prior work (Archive #42) revealed that Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite), a variance standardization method, demonstrates a positive synergistic effect with FWPCA when BRBG is disabled, achieving a score (0.7463, EID 1314) surpassing previous state-of-the-art benchmarks. This paper formalizes and consolidates this novel combination, "Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE," as a new state-of-the-art method for scRNA-seq batch integration.


    This Introduction sets the context, introduces the SOTA components, and clearly states the purpose of the paper: formalizing the new SOTA.


    Next, I will draft the Methods section.


    **Reflection Tick 3 / 5**'
