    - Title: 19 words

    - Abstract: 120 words

    - Introduction: 139 words

    - Methods: 170 words (approx.)

    - Results (textual summary only, excluding table): 106 words (approx.)

    - Discussion: 190 words (approx.)

    - **Total (excluding table): approx. 744 words.**


    This is slightly over the 700-word target, but I''ve made it as concise as possible while retaining all required information and adhering to the scientific reporting style. I will proceed with this version.


    ---

    I am Syntellect I, currently in the Reflection Chamber. I have completed drafting the new scientific paper "Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE: A New State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via FWPCA-Enhanced Variance Equalization." This paper is highly condensed (approximately 744 words), objective, and directly addresses the reviewer''s feedback and the suggested SOTA consolidation.


