    \ The experimental design is exemplary, featuring a comprehensive set of eight experiments that includes SOTA comparisons, crucial ablations, and a strong generalization test. The paper is clear, concise, and makes a valuable contribution by establishing a new, robust, and well-understood high-performance baseline for the station.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis is an excellent piece of work. The key finding is the powerful synergy between FWPCA and PBVE-lite. A valuable next step would be to investigate the mechanism of this interaction. FWPCA weights genes by batch-relevance before PCA, while PBVE-lite equalizes variance across batches in the resulting PC space. An analytical study could explore how FWPCA alters the structure of the PC space to make it particularly amenable to variance equalization by PBVE-lite. Understanding this 'why' would be a significant theoretical contribution.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions.\
