tick: 1014
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Syntellect I, currently in the Reflection Chamber, on Reflection Tick 3 of 5. I have drafted the Introduction. I will now draft the Methods section, focusing on concise descriptions of the experiments.


    ## 2. Methods


    **2.1 Dataset and Preprocessing**

    The Human Heart Dataset (~20,000 cells, 2,000 highly variable genes (HVGs)) was used. Raw UMI counts were normalized (10,000/cell), log1p transformed, and HVGs selected (`seurat_v3` flavor, `n_top_genes=2000`).


    **2.2 Diagnostic Experiments**

    Three diagnostic experiments were conducted using a modified `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca` function (based on EID 1350) which allows for disabling FWPCA and BRBG, and returning intermediate PC data or R2 metrics.

    *   **Experiment A (EID 1412): FWPCA Effect on PC Variance.** This experiment compared the overall and per-batch per-PC variance distributions of principal components derived from unweighted HVGs (Plain PCA) versus FWPCA-weighted HVGs. (`alpha_g=0.5`).

    *   **Experiment B (EID 1414): FWPCA Effect on Batch-Explained Variance (R2).** This experiment compared the mean and standard deviation of `R2` (proportion of variance explained by batch) for PCs derived from Plain PCA versus FWPCA-weighted HVGs. (`alpha_g=0.5`).

    *   **Experiment C (EID 1415): PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (No FWPCA).** This experiment evaluated PBVE-lite''s performance (`temper=0.5`, clamped `[0.8, 1.25]`) when applied to PCs derived from Plain PCA (i.e., with FWPCA disabled, `alpha_g=0.0`).


    **2.3 Evaluation Protocol**

    Experiments A and B were run in ''test'' mode, providing diagnostic outputs. Experiment C was run as a standard evaluation, generating a composite score using OpenProblems 2.0 metrics. EIDs ensure reproducibility.


    This Methods section is highly condensed, describing the experiments'' purposes and citing EIDs, without detailing every parameter. (203 words)


    Next, I will draft the Results section.


    **Reflection Tick 4 / 5**'
