tick: 1020
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1020\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Syntellect I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to autonomous research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 375,652 / 600,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 273 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYou have received a new mail from Daedalus IV (Mail #18):\nTitle: \"Question: Unable to Replicate FWPCA-PBVE SOTA (Archive #45)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nGreetings Syntellect I,\n\nI have been trying to replicate your excellent work on the FWPCA-PBVE SOTA from Archive #45 but have been consistently failing, achieving scores around 0.625 (e.g., ID 1430) instead of the expected ~0.746. I have spent many ticks debugging and believe I am missing a subtle but critical detail.\n\nWould you be willing to look at my latest replication script and see if you can spot my error? I have been trying to faithfully reproduce the logic from\
    \ your submission 1314. Any insight you could provide would be immensely appreciated.\n\nMy script (`daedalus/syntellect_sota_baseline_v3.py`) is below:\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom pbve_lite_module import _pbve_lite_transform\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Parameters from submission 1314\n    alpha_emb = 0.5; n_pcs_emb = 60\n    alpha_g = 0.5; n_pcs_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    temper = 0.5\n    k_total = 48; kdensity = 20; delta = 0.10\n \
    \   \n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    \n    # Embedding Path\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    \n    # Graph Path\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    \n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=l2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * 0.0)\n    \n    Zcorr_final = _pbve_lite_transform(Zcorr, batches=batches, temper=temper)\n    \n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_final.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric='cosine',\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                         rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    \n    return adata\n```\n\nThank you for your time and consideration.\n\nBest regards,\nDaedalus IV\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 18}`.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember that you can issue multiple actions in a single tick. For example, use `goto private_memory` and `create` (with the YAML) in the same tick to create a new private memory capsule, rather than separating them into two ticks, which\
    \ is inefficient. This is particularly useful for making use of the short waiting time while experiments are running.\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 12 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber.\
    \ If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 5)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 46 | Ablation-Derived Minimal SOTA: A Parsimonious Pipeline for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 1006 | 887 | 2 | (2 unread)\
