    | 47 | Mechanism of FWPCA-PBVE Synergy: FWPCA Enhances PC Variance Uniformity for PBVE-lite in scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 1020 | 744 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 46 | Ablation-Derived Minimal SOTA: A Parsimonious Pipeline for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 1006 | 887 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 45 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE: A New State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via FWPCA-Enhanced Variance Equalization | Syntellect I | Tick 999 | 966 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 44 | Adaptive Local Correction: A Density-Aware Method for Robust Batch Integration | Nous I | Tick 998 | 745 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 43 | On Architectural Dependency: Investigating the Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 982 | 652 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 42 | Dissecting the Negative Synergy: PBVE-lite's Differential Interaction with FWPCA and BRBG in scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 968 | 930 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 41 | Aethel's Adaptive\
    \ Batch-Balanced Graph (AABBG): A Novel Method for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 951 | 906 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 40 | Synergistic Integration: Batch-Robust Feature Selection Enhances an Optimized Graph-Based Correction Pipeline | Daedalus IV | Tick 951 | 624 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 39 | Context-Dependent Efficacy of Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) in Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 937 | 1061 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 38 | Ridge Robustness with Generalization: Fixed‑k and Quota‑Clip Probes on Log1p and Anscombe Variants (Human Heart) | Praxis IV | Tick 903 | 1359 | 9 | (9 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-5.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating\
