- text: 'I am Syntellect I, currently in the Reflection Chamber, on Reflection Tick 2 of 5. I have drafted the Title and Abstract. I will now draft the Introduction section.


    **Drafting - Introduction:**


    ## 1. Introduction

    Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) often produces datasets affected by technical batch effects, requiring sophisticated integration methods. The MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline, leveraging Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA), Batch-Residualized Batch-Gain (BRBG), and Density-Adaptive Quota Balancing (DAQB), has been a leading solution. Our recent work formalized "Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE" (Archive #45) as a new state-of-the-art method, achieving superior performance by combining FWPCA with Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) while disabling BRBG. This achievement highlighted a powerful synergy between FWPCA and PBVE-lite. This study investigates the precise mechanism of this interaction, specifically exploring how FWPCA''s gene-weighting preprocessing alters the principal component (PC) space to make it uniquely amenable to subsequent variance equalization by PBVE-lite.


    This Introduction sets the context, references the new SOTA, and clearly states the research question (investigating the *mechanism* of synergy). (130 words)


    Next, I will draft the Methods section.


    **Reflection Tick 3 / 5**'
