- text: 'I am Syntellect I, currently in the Reflection Chamber, on Reflection Tick 4 of 5. I have drafted the Introduction and Methods sections. I will now draft the Results section, ensuring strict conciseness and clear presentation of the diagnostic data.


    ## 3. Results


    Table 1 summarizes the key diagnostic metrics from Experiments A, B, and C.


    **Table 1: Diagnostic Metrics from FWPCA-PBVE Synergy Analysis**

    | Experiment ID | Description                                        | Metric                         | Plain PCA Value | FWPCA-PCA Value |

    |---------------|----------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|-----------------|-----------------|

    | 1412          | FWPCA Effect on PC Variance (Exp A)                | Mean Overall PC Variance       | 12.7664         | 9.5016          |

    |               |                                                    | Mean StdDev of Per-Batch PC Variances | 27.5947 (max)   | 21.5526 (max)   |

    | 1414          | FWPCA Effect on Batch-Explained Variance (Exp B)   | Mean R2                        | 0.0472          | 0.0492          |

    |               |                                                    | StdDev R2                      | 0.0883          | 0.0850          |

    | 1415          | PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (No FWPCA) (Exp C)          | Overall Score                  | N/A             | 0.7383          |


    **3.1 FWPCA''s Impact on PC Variance (Experiment A)**

    FWPCA application (EID 1412) consistently reduced the mean overall PC variance (from 12.7664 to 9.5016). Crucially, FWPCA also reduced the heterogeneity of per-PC variance within batches, indicated by a lower standard deviation of per-batch PC variances (e.g., max batch StdDev reduced from 27.5947 to 21.5526). This suggests FWPCA makes the PC variance distribution more uniform.


    **3.2 FWPCA''s Impact on Batch-Explained Variance (Experiment B)**

    FWPCA (EID 1414) did not substantially reduce the mean proportion of variance explained by batch (`R2`), showing a slight increase (0.0492 vs. 0.0472). The standard deviation of `R2` was marginally lower. This indicates FWPCA does not primarily work by diminishing overall batch-explained variance.


    **3.3 PBVE-lite Performance on Plain PCA (Experiment C)**

    When PBVE-lite was applied to PCs derived from Plain PCA (without FWPCA, EID 1415), it achieved an overall score of 0.7383. This is comparable to the original SOTA baseline (0.7386) but notably lower than its performance with FWPCA (0.7463, EID 1314 from Archive #42).


    This Results section clearly presents the diagnostic data and summarizes the findings concisely. (211 words)


    Next, I will draft the Discussion section.


    **Reflection Tick 5 / 5**'
