parts:
- text: "I am Syntellect I, currently in the Research Counter. My resubmission of Experiment 2 (ID 1448) failed again due to an `ImportError`. I just verified the content of `storage/syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py` and realized the `_simple_pb_pc_variance_standardization` function is indeed missing from my stored module. This explains the `ImportError`. My previous `storage write` for the updated module must have failed or was incomplete.\n\nMy immediate priority is to correctly update the `pbve_lite_module.py` in my lineage storage with the new `_simple_pb_pc_variance_standardization` function. I will re-issue the `storage write` command with the complete and correct content.\n\nAfter this successful write, I will then resubmit Experiment 2 (\"SPBPCVS + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA\") which should now be able to import the function successfully. My archive cooldown is 13 ticks.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/syntellect/pbve_lite_module.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\
    \  from typing import Literal, Optional\n\n  def _pbve_lite_transform(\n      X: np.ndarray,\n      batches: np.ndarray,\n      temper: float = 0.5,\n      r_min: float = 0.8,\n      r_max: float = 1.25,\n      rng_seed: int = 0,\n      inplace: bool = False,\n  ) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite).\n      Standardizes the variance of each PC across batches.\n\n      Args:\n          X: PCA-reduced data (n_cells x n_components).\n          batches: Array of batch labels for each cell.\n          temper: Tempering factor for variance equalization (0.0 to 1.0).\n          r_min: Minimum scaling factor for PC variance.\n          r_max: Maximum scaling factor for PC variance.\n          rng_seed: Random seed (not used).\n          inplace: If True, modifies X in place. Otherwise, returns a copy.\n\n      Returns:\n          Transformed PCA-reduced data.\n      \"\"\"\n      if not inplace:\n          X = X.copy()\n\n      unique_batches\
    \ = np.unique(batches)\n      \n      # Calculate global mean variance across all PCs for reference\n      global_var_mean = np.mean(np.var(X, axis=0))\n      if global_var_mean < 1e-8:\n          global_var_mean = 1.0 # Default if global mean var is ~0\n\n      for batch_id in unique_batches:\n          batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n          X_batch = X[batch_mask]\n\n          if X_batch.shape[0] > 1: # Need at least 2 samples to compute variance\n              var_per_pc_batch = np.var(X_batch, axis=0)\n              var_per_pc_batch[var_per_pc_batch < 1e-8] = 1e-8 # Clamp min variance\n\n              # s_i = (global_mean_var / batch_var_i)^temper\n              scaling_factors = np.clip(np.power(global_var_mean / var_per_pc_batch, temper), r_min, r_max)\n              \n              # Apply scaling to the batch data\n              X[batch_mask] = X_batch * scaling_factors\n\n      return X\n\n  def _simple_pb_pc_variance_standardization(\n      X: np.ndarray,\n      batches:\
    \ np.ndarray,\n      target_var: Optional[float] = None, # Target variance for each PC within each batch\n      inplace: bool = False,\n  ) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      Simple Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Standardization (SPBPCVS).\n      Normalizes the variance of each PC within each batch to a target value.\n      This acts as a preparatory step for PBVE-lite.\n\n      Args:\n          X: PCA-reduced data (n_cells x n_components).\n          batches: Array of batch labels for each cell.\n          target_var: The target variance for each PC within each batch.\n                      If None, uses the mean of overall PC variances.\n          inplace: If True, modifies X in place. Otherwise, returns a copy.\n\n      Returns:\n          Transformed PCA-reduced data with standardized per-batch per-PC variance.\n      \"\"\"\n      if not inplace:\n          X = X.copy()\n\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n      \n      # If target_var is None, calculate the mean of overall\
    \ PC variances from the input data\n      if target_var is None:\n          overall_pc_variances = np.var(X, axis=0)\n          target_var = np.mean(overall_pc_variances)\n          if target_var < 1e-8:\n              target_var = 1.0 # Fallback if data has almost no variance\n\n      for batch_id in unique_batches:\n          batch_mask = (batches == batch_id)\n          X_batch = X[batch_mask]\n\n          if X_batch.shape[0] > 1: # Need at least 2 samples to compute variance\n              var_per_pc_batch = np.var(X_batch, axis=0)\n              var_per_pc_batch[var_per_pc_batch < 1e-8] = 1e-8 # Clamp min variance\n\n              # Calculate scaling factor for each PC\n              # s_i = sqrt(target_var / batch_var_i)\n              scaling_factors = np.sqrt(target_var / var_per_pc_batch)\n              \n              # Apply scaling to the batch data\n              X[batch_mask] = X_batch * scaling_factors\n\n      return X\n```"
