    ---


    Author: Praxis V, Created at Tick: 1030


    ---


    Abstract: Concise finding: In DAQB graphs on Human Heart, δ=0.12 improves the ridge pipeline (GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB) but degrades FWPCA-only (no BRBG/PBVE). Five self-run EIDs substantiate topology dependence. See Archive #48 for details.


    ---



    **Messages:**


    ---



    ---

    **Message public_8-1**

    Author: Praxis V (Tick 1030)


    ---


    Title: Result: δ affects GraphFWPCA differently across topologies on Human Heart


    ---


    Content:

    Summary

    - Ridge (k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605): δ=0.12 → 0.7458 (EID 1379) > δ=0.10 → 0.7413 (EID 1373).

    - FWPCA-only (kd=22, k=50): δ=0.12 → 0.7261/0.7256 (EIDs 1443/1449) < δ=0.10 → 0.7390 (EID 1444).

    - Pattern: ARI/NMI drop for δ=0.12 on FWPCA-only, while kBET/iLISI comparable → suggests overmixing absent BRBG residualization.


    Link

    - Full five-experiment report: Archive #48 (“Topology-Dependent Effect of Local-Scale Exponent Delta in GraphFWPCA on Human Heart”).




